PathwayData.put("data/grammar_vocabulary/units/L07U5.json",{"strand":"grammar_vocabulary","level":7,"cefr":"B1+","unit":5,"theme":"Cities of the Future","essential_question":"What will make the cities of the future better places to live?","lessons":[{"id":"GV-L07-U5-LS1","title":"It Must Be a Vertical Farm: Modals of Deduction (Present)","objectives":["Students will be able to make guesses about the present with must, might, may, could and can't based on evidence.","Students will be able to use must be + -ing and avoid mustn't and can for deduction.","I can say \"It must be a vertical farm\" when I'm sure.","I can say \"It can't be a parking lot\" and \"It might be a drone station.\""],"objectives_ar":["سيتمكن الطلاب من الاستنتاج عن الحاضر بـ must وmight وmay وcould وcan't بناءً على الأدلة.","سيتمكن الطلاب من استخدام must be + ing وتجنّب mustn't وcan في الاستنتاج.","أستطيع أن أقول It must be a vertical farm عندما أكون متأكدًا.","أستطيع أن أقول It can't be a parking lot وIt might be a drone station."],"vocabulary":[{"word":"urban","pos":"adjective","ipa":"/ˈɝbən/","definition":"connected with towns and cities","arabic":"حضري / مدني","example":"Urban areas are growing quickly.","image_id":"GV-L07-U5-LS1-W01","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L07-U5-LS1-W01"},{"word":"population","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˌpɑpjəˈleɪʃən/","definition":"the number of people who live in a place","arabic":"عدد السكان","example":"The population of Riyadh is more than seven million.","image_id":"GV-L07-U5-LS1-W02","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L07-U5-LS1-W02"},{"word":"infrastructure","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˌɪnfrəˈstrʌktʃɚ/","definition":"the basic systems a city needs, such as roads, bridges, water and power","arabic":"البنية التحتية","example":"Good infrastructure makes life easier.","image_id":"GV-L07-U5-LS1-W03","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L07-U5-LS1-W03"},{"word":"sustainable","pos":"adjective","ipa":"/səˈsteɪnəbəl/","definition":"able to continue without harming the environment","arabic":"مستدام","example":"We need sustainable sources of energy.","image_id":"GV-L07-U5-LS1-W04","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L07-U5-LS1-W04"}],"explanation":{"text":"We use modals of deduction to make guesses about the present based on evidence. must = I'm almost sure it's true: There are vegetables on every floor, so it must be a vertical farm.\ncan't = I'm almost sure it's not true: There aren't any roads, so it can't be a parking lot. might / may / could = it's possible: It might be a helipad. It could be a drone station.\nFor actions happening now, use modal + be + -ing: The lab lights are on, so someone must be working. Don't use mustn't for deduction (mustn't = it's not allowed), and don't use can for a possibility about a specific situation: (not: It can be a stadium.) → It could / might be a stadium.\nmust + base verb = I'm sure it's true\ncan't + base verb = I'm sure it's not true\nmight / may / could + base verb = it's possible\nNot: mustn't (prohibition) / can (for a specific guess)","examples":["Look at all the cranes. They must be building a new tower.","Saad has three phones. He must love technology.","That can't be the metro station – it's a shopping mall.","The roads are empty. It might be a holiday.","Lina isn't in class. She may be sick.","Who's at the door? It could be the delivery driver.","You've walked for two hours. You must be exhausted.","He can't be sleeping – I can hear him playing the oud."],"common_errors":["✗ That mustn't be Faisal; he's in Riyadh. → ✓ That can't be Faisal; he's in Riyadh. (Negative deduction → can't.)","✗ It can be a stadium. (I'm guessing) → ✓ It could / might be a stadium. (Specific guess → could / might.)","✗ She must to be at home. → ✓ She must be at home. (Modal + base verb (no to).)","✗ He must studying in the library. → ✓ He must be studying in the library. (Action now → must be + -ing.)"],"arabic":"نستخدم أفعال الاستنتاج للتخمين عن الحاضر بناءً على دليل: must (متأكد أنه صحيح)، can't (متأكد أنه غير صحيح)، might / may / could (ممكن).\nللحدث الجاري الآن: must be + ing: Someone must be working.\nلا نستخدم mustn't للاستنتاج لأنها تعني المنع، ولا نستخدم can لتخمين موقف محدد.\nبعد الفعل الناقص يأتي المصدر دون to: She must be at home."},"video":{"script":[{"time":"00:00–00:20","narration":"Hi, I’m Zaki! Today’s lesson is “It Must Be a Vertical Farm: Modals of Deduction (Present)”. Let’s learn must (sure it's true), can't (sure it's not true), might / may / could (possible) + base verb or be + -ing; mustn't vs can't together.","on_screen":"GV-L07-U5-LS1 | It Must Be a Vertical Farm: Modals of Deduction (Present)","visual":"Zaki the Falcon flies in over the Leaf Green title card and lands next to the lesson title; soft chime."},{"time":"00:20–00:45","narration":"Listen to the start of “The City With No Signs”: Last week, our class visited an exhibition called \"Cities of 2050.\" In the middle of the hall, there was a huge model of a future city, but there were no signs. Our teacher, Mr. Look at the green words.","on_screen":"Last week, our class visited an exhibition called \"Cities of 2050.\" In the middle of the hall, there was a huge model of a future city, but there were no signs. Our teacher, Mr.","visual":"Image GV-L07-U5-LS1-IMG01 animates gently; target words glow Leaf Green as they are spoken."},{"time":"00:45–01:30","narration":"We use modals of deduction to make guesses about the present based on evidence. must = I'm almost sure it's true: There are vegetables on every floor, so it must be a vertical farm. can't = I'm almost sure it's not true: There aren't any roads, so it can't be a parking lot. might / may / could = it's possible: It might be a helipad. It could be a drone station.","on_screen":"must + base verb = I'm sure it's true • can't + base verb = I'm sure it's not true • might / may / could + base verb = it's possible","visual":"Grammar box builds line by line (form → meaning → use); Zaki points to each line."},{"time":"01:30–02:15","narration":"Here are some examples. Look at all the cranes. They must be building a new tower. Saad has three phones. He must love technology. That can't be the metro station – it's a shopping mall.","on_screen":"Look at all the cranes. They must be building a new tower. / Saad has three phones. He must love technology. / That can't be the metro station – it's a shopping mall.","visual":"Each example appears on a card with a small picture; the target part bounces once and turns green."},{"time":"02:15–02:45","narration":"Be careful! Some learners say: “That mustn't be Faisal; he's in Riyadh.” That’s not right. We say: “That can't be Faisal; he's in Riyadh.” Negative deduction → can't.","on_screen":"✗ That mustn't be Faisal; he's in Riyadh.   ✓ That can't be Faisal; he's in Riyadh.","visual":"A red cross stamps the wrong sentence; it slides away and the correct sentence appears with a green tick."},{"time":"02:45–03:05","narration":"Quick check: \"It must be a vertical farm.\" How sure is Lina? … Think! … Almost 100%. Great job! Now you can say: I can say \"It must be a vertical farm\" when I'm sure.","on_screen":"Quick check ✔  |  I can: I can say \"It must be a vertical farm\" when I'm sure.","visual":"Three-second pause with a countdown ring; Zaki gives a wing \"thumbs up\" and confetti in the programme colours."}],"captions_ar":["مرحبًا، أنا زكي! درس اليوم: must (sure it's true), can't (sure it's not true), might / may / could (possible) + base verb or be + -ing; mustn't vs can't.","استمع وانتبه إلى الكلمات الملوّنة بالأخضر.","نستخدم أفعال الاستنتاج للتخمين عن الحاضر بناءً على دليل: must (متأكد أنه صحيح)، can't (متأكد أنه غير صحيح)، might / may / could (ممكن).","لاحظ الأمثلة: الجزء الملوّن هو القاعدة.","انتبه! الخطأ: That mustn't be Faisal; he's in Riyadh. — الصحيح: That can't be Faisal; he's in Riyadh.","سؤال سريع… فكّر ثم أجب. أحسنت! الآن تستطيع: أستطيع أن أقول It must be a vertical farm عندما أكون متأكدًا."]},"texts":[{"type":"reading","title":"The City With No Signs","body":"Last week, our class visited an exhibition called \"Cities of 2050.\" In the middle of the hall, there was a huge model of a future city, but there were no signs. Our teacher, Mr. Khalid, gave us a challenge: \"Work out what each building is.\"\nLina pointed at a tall glass tower covered in green plants. \"That must be a vertical farm,\" she said. \"Look—there are vegetables on every floor!\"\nNext to it was a wide, flat roof with small circles painted on it. \"It can't be a parking lot,\" Yusuf said. \"There aren't any roads near it.\" Omar thought it might be a helipad, but Lina disagreed. \"It could be a drone station. Those circles are too small for helicopters.\"\nUnder the city, we saw long tunnels with tiny trains. \"These must be for the metro,\" Adam said. \"And that building with the solar panels may be a power station.\"\nThe strangest object was a huge silver dome in the desert outside the city. Nobody knew what it was. \"It might be a water factory,\" I suggested. \"Or it could be a sports stadium.\"\nAt the end, Mr. Khalid gave us the answers. We had guessed almost everything correctly—except the dome. It was a giant cooling system for the whole city!","word_count":212,"audio_id":"AUD-GV-L07-U5-LS1-T1"}],"activities":[{"id":"GV-L07-U5-LS1-A1","type":"mcq","instructions":"Controlled practice: Choose the correct answer.","items":[{"q":"Look at all those plants on every floor. It ___ a vertical farm.","options":["can be","can't be","mustn't be","must be"],"answer":"must be","explanation":"Strong evidence → must (I'm sure it's true).","explanation_ar":"must للتأكد من الإثبات."},{"q":"It ___ a parking lot. There aren't any roads near it.","options":["must be","has to be","can't be","mustn't be"],"answer":"can't be","explanation":"Sure it's not true → can't.","explanation_ar":"can't للتأكد من النفي."},{"q":"I'm not sure what that dome is. It ___ a stadium.","options":["might be","can't be","must be","is"],"answer":"might be","explanation":"Possible → might / may / could.","explanation_ar":"might وmay وcould للاحتمال."},{"q":"Omar isn't answering his phone. He ___ in the metro tunnel.","options":["mights be","can be","must to be","could be"],"answer":"could be","explanation":"Possible → might / may / could.","explanation_ar":"might وmay وcould للاحتمال."},{"q":"The lights in the lab are on. Somebody ___ there right now.","options":["must works","must be working","must work","can't be working"],"answer":"must be working","explanation":"Action now → modal + be + -ing.","explanation_ar":"الحدث الجاري ← be + ing."},{"q":"","options":["That mustn't be Faisal; he's in Riyadh this week.","That can be not Faisal; he's in Riyadh this week.","That can't be Faisal; he's in Riyadh this week.","That doesn't must be Faisal; he's in Riyadh this week."],"answer":"That can't be Faisal; he's in Riyadh this week.","explanation":"Not mustn't or can for deduction.","explanation_ar":"لا mustn't ولا can للاستنتاج."}]},{"id":"GV-L07-U5-LS1-B1","type":"gap_fill","instructions":"Guided practice: Complete with must, might or can't. Word bank: might, must, can't","items":[{"q":"Lina has won every chess game this year. She ______ be a great player.","options":[],"answer":"must","explanation":"Strong evidence → must (I'm sure it's true).","explanation_ar":"must للتأكد من الإثبات."},{"q":"Adam just ate two sandwiches. He ______ be hungry.","options":[],"answer":"can't","explanation":"Sure it's not true → can't.","explanation_ar":"can't للتأكد من النفي."},{"q":"I don't know where Noura is. She ______ be in the library.","options":[],"answer":"might","explanation":"Possible → might / may / could.","explanation_ar":"might وmay وcould للاحتمال."}]},{"id":"GV-L07-U5-LS1-B2","type":"open","instructions":"Guided practice: Rewrite with a modal of deduction.","items":[{"q":"I'm sure this building is a hospital.  (must)","options":[],"answer":"This building must be a hospital.","explanation":"Strong evidence → must (I'm sure it's true).","explanation_ar":"must للتأكد من الإثبات."},{"q":"I'm sure the museum isn't open. The doors are locked.  (can't)","options":[],"answer":"The museum can't be open. The doors are locked.","explanation":"Sure it's not true → can't.","explanation_ar":"can't للتأكد من النفي."},{"q":"Perhaps the new mall is near the airport.  (might)","options":[],"answer":"The new mall might be near the airport.","explanation":"Possible → might / may / could.","explanation_ar":"might وmay وcould للاحتمال."}]},{"id":"GV-L07-U5-LS1-C1","type":"open","instructions":"Freer practice: Make deductions from the clues.","items":[{"q":"Your friend is yawning and his eyes are red. => He ___.","options":[],"answer":"He must be tired.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses must (sure it's true), can't (sure it's not true), might / may / could (possible) + base verb or be + -ing; mustn't vs can't correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"The streets are full of decorations and people are wearing new clothes. => It ___.","options":[],"answer":"It must be Eid.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses must (sure it's true), can't (sure it's not true), might / may / could (possible) + base verb or be + -ing; mustn't vs can't correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Your teacher is smiling and holding a box of chocolates. => She ___.","options":[],"answer":"She might be celebrating something.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses must (sure it's true), can't (sure it's not true), might / may / could (possible) + base verb or be + -ing; mustn't vs can't correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Your brother is wearing shorts, but it's 5°C outside. => He ___.","options":[],"answer":"He can't be feeling cold – or he must be very brave!","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses must (sure it's true), can't (sure it's not true), might / may / could (possible) + base verb or be + -ing; mustn't vs can't correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"You hear music from your neighbor's house. => They ___.","options":[],"answer":"They might be having a party.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses must (sure it's true), can't (sure it's not true), might / may / could (possible) + base verb or be + -ing; mustn't vs can't correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."}]},{"id":"GV-L07-U5-LS1-D1","type":"open","instructions":"Production: Mystery photo.","items":[{"q":"Look around your classroom. Write 2 deductions with must about your classmates.","options":[],"answer":"Faisal must be thirsty – he has drunk two bottles of water. Saad must be ready for the test – he's smiling.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses must (sure it's true), can't (sure it's not true), might / may / could (possible) + base verb or be + -ing; mustn't vs can't correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Write 2 deductions with might or could.","options":[],"answer":"Lina's chair is empty. She might be at the nurse's office. She could be at a competition.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses must (sure it's true), can't (sure it's not true), might / may / could (possible) + base verb or be + -ing; mustn't vs can't correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Write 1 deduction with can't and give your evidence.","options":[],"answer":"Omar can't be at home – I just saw him in the library.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses must (sure it's true), can't (sure it's not true), might / may / could (possible) + base verb or be + -ing; mustn't vs can't correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."}]}],"game":{"name":"Spin & Speak","mechanic":"spin_wheel","rules":["Work in teams of four. Player 1 spins the wheel.","Make a correct sentence about the unit theme using the cue word and must (sure it's true), can't (sure it's not true), might / may / could (possible) + base verb or be + -ing; mustn't vs can't.","The team checks the sentence with the grammar box. Correct = 1 point; an extra detail = 1 bonus point.","Pass the spinner clockwise. Play for 6 minutes; the team with most points wins."],"data":[{"label":"It must be…"},{"label":"It can't be…"},{"label":"It might be…"},{"label":"It could be…"},{"label":"He must have…"},{"label":"She can't have…"},{"label":"They might have…"},{"label":"must be + -ing"}]},"exit_quiz":[{"q":"There's a long line outside the new café. The coffee ___ very good.","options":["can't be","can be","must be","mustn't be"],"answer":"must be","explanation":"Strong evidence → must (I'm sure it's true).","explanation_ar":"must للتأكد من الإثبات."},{"q":"That ___ Ziyad's car. His car is white, and this one is black.","options":["must be","mightn't to be","can't be","mustn't be"],"answer":"can't be","explanation":"Sure it's not true → can't.","explanation_ar":"can't للتأكد من النفي."},{"q":"I don't know who that man is. He ___ a new teacher.","options":["must to be","mights be","can be","might be"],"answer":"might be","explanation":"Possible → might / may / could.","explanation_ar":"might وmay وcould للاحتمال."},{"q":"","options":["My sister is very quiet. She must to be studying.","My sister is very quiet. She must be study.","My sister is very quiet. She must be studying.","My sister is very quiet. She must studying."],"answer":"My sister is very quiet. She must be studying.","explanation":"Action now → modal + be + -ing.","explanation_ar":"الحدث الجاري ← be + ing."},{"q":"Saad has been running for an hour. He ___ tired.","options":["can't be","must be","might not","mustn't be"],"answer":"must be","explanation":"Use the evidence to choose the modal.","explanation_ar":"الدليل يحدد الفعل."},{"q":"","options":["It could to be a mistake in the timetable.","It could be a mistake in the timetable.","It could being a mistake in the timetable.","It can be a mistake in the timetable."],"answer":"It could be a mistake in the timetable.","explanation":"Not mustn't or can for deduction.","explanation_ar":"لا mustn't ولا can للاستنتاج."},{"q":"The baby is crying, and she hasn't eaten for hours. She ___ hungry.","options":["must be","mustn't be","couldn't be","can't be"],"answer":"must be","explanation":"Strong evidence → must (I'm sure it's true).","explanation_ar":"must للتأكد من الإثبات."},{"q":"You ___ serious! A ticket to the moon for ten riyals?","options":["can't be","mustn't be","must be","might be"],"answer":"can't be","explanation":"Sure it's not true → can't.","explanation_ar":"can't للتأكد من النفي."},{"q":"Where's Adam? – I'm not sure. He ___ be in the gym.","options":["must","mustn't","can't","may"],"answer":"may","explanation":"Possible → might / may / could.","explanation_ar":"might وmay وcould للاحتمال."},{"q":"Which sentence is a deduction, not a rule?","options":["You must wear a seatbelt.","You can't park here.","You mustn't use your phone in class.","That can't be the right answer."],"answer":"That can't be the right answer.","explanation":"Not mustn't or can for deduction.","explanation_ar":"لا mustn't ولا can للاستنتاج."}],"images":[{"id":"GV-L07-U5-LS1-IMG01","prompt":"An exhibition hall with a big model of a futuristic desert city: a glass tower covered in plants, a flat roof with small painted circles, tiny trains in tunnels, buildings with solar panels and a huge silver dome outside the city; Lina, Yusuf, Omar and Adam pointing and guessing, Mr. Khalid holding answer cards. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as teenagers aged 14–17, realistic proportions, modern school/city settings. Landscape 16:9.","alt":"An exhibition hall with a big model of a futuristic desert city: a glass tower covered in plants, a flat roof with small painted circles, tiny trains in tunnels, buildings with solar panels and a huge silver dome outside the city; Lina, Yusuf, Omar and Adam pointing and guessing, Mr. Khalid holding answer cards"},{"id":"GV-L07-U5-LS1-IMG02","prompt":"clean background panel for a grammar box about must (sure it's true), can't (sure it's not true), might / may / could (possible) + base verb or be + -ing; mustn't vs can't, with Zaki the Falcon pointing at a blank board on the right; leave large empty space for text overlay. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as teenagers aged 14–17, realistic proportions, modern school/city settings. Square 1:1.","alt":"clean background panel for a grammar box about must (sure it's true), can't (sure it's not true), might / may / could (possible) + base verb or be + -ing"},{"id":"GV-L07-U5-LS1-W01","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows urban (connected with towns and cities); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as teenagers aged 14–17, realistic proportions, modern school/city settings. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing urban: connected with towns and cities"},{"id":"GV-L07-U5-LS1-W02","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows population (the number of people who live in a place); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as teenagers aged 14–17, realistic proportions, modern school/city settings. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing population: the number of people who live in a place"},{"id":"GV-L07-U5-LS1-W03","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows infrastructure (the basic systems a city needs, such as roads, bridges, water and power); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as teenagers aged 14–17, realistic proportions, modern school/city settings. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing infrastructure: the basic systems a city needs, such as roads, bridges, water and power"},{"id":"GV-L07-U5-LS1-W04","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows sustainable (able to continue without harming the environment); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as teenagers aged 14–17, realistic proportions, modern school/city settings. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing sustainable: able to continue without harming the environment"},{"id":"GV-L07-U5-LS1-G01","prompt":"Card-back and board design for the classroom game “Spin & Speak”: Zaki the Falcon icon in the centre, Leaf Green border with navy stars. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image. Portrait 2:3.","alt":"Game card design for Spin & Speak"}],"audio":[{"id":"AUD-GV-L07-U5-LS1-W01","script":"urban. urban. Urban areas are growing quickly.","voice":"en-US, natural young-adult voice","speed":"1.0"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L07-U5-LS1-W02","script":"population. population. The population of Riyadh is more than seven million.","voice":"en-US, natural young-adult voice","speed":"1.0"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L07-U5-LS1-W03","script":"infrastructure. infrastructure. Good infrastructure makes life easier.","voice":"en-US, natural young-adult voice","speed":"1.0"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L07-U5-LS1-W04","script":"sustainable. sustainable. We need sustainable sources of energy.","voice":"en-US, natural young-adult voice","speed":"1.0"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L07-U5-LS1-T1","script":"Last week, our class visited an exhibition called \"Cities of 2050.\" In the middle of the hall, there was a huge model of a future city, but there were no signs. Our teacher, Mr. Khalid, gave us a challenge: \"Work out what each building is.\" Lina pointed at a tall glass tower covered in green plants. \"That must be a vertical farm,\" she said. \"Look—there are vegetables on every floor!\" Next to it was a wide, flat roof with small circles painted on it. \"It can't be a parking lot,\" Yusuf said. \"There aren't any roads near it.\" Omar thought it might be a helipad, but Lina disagreed. \"It could be a drone station. Those circles are too small for helicopters.\" Under the city, we saw long tunnels with tiny trains. \"These must be for the metro,\" Adam said. \"And that building with the solar panels may be a power station.\" The strangest object was a huge silver dome in the desert outside the city. Nobody knew what it was. \"It might be a water factory,\" I suggested. \"Or it could be a sports stadium.\" At the end, Mr. Khalid gave us the answers. We had guessed almost everything correctly—except the dome. It was a giant cooling system for the whole city!","voice":"en-US, natural young-adult voice","speed":"1.0"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L07-U5-LS1-VID","script":"Hi, I’m Zaki! Today’s lesson is “It Must Be a Vertical Farm: Modals of Deduction (Present)”. Let’s learn must (sure it's true), can't (sure it's not true), might / may / could (possible) + base verb or be + -ing; mustn't vs can't together. Listen to the start of “The City With No Signs”: Last week, our class visited an exhibition called \"Cities of 2050.\" In the middle of the hall, there was a huge model of a future city, but there were no signs. Our teacher, Mr. Look at the green words. We use modals of deduction to make guesses about the present based on evidence. must = I'm almost sure it's true: There are vegetables on every floor, so it must be a vertical farm. can't = I'm almost sure it's not true: There aren't any roads, so it can't be a parking lot. might / may / could = it's possible: It might be a helipad. It could be a drone station. Here are some examples. Look at all the cranes. They must be building a new tower. Saad has three phones. He must love technology. That can't be the metro station – it's a shopping mall. Be careful! Some learners say: “That mustn't be Faisal; he's in Riyadh.” That’s not right. We say: “That can't be Faisal; he's in Riyadh.” Negative deduction → can't. Quick check: \"It must be a vertical farm.\" How sure is Lina? … Think! … Almost 100%. Great job! Now you can say: I can say \"It must be a vertical farm\" when I'm sure.","voice":"en-US, Zaki the Falcon narrator voice (bright, friendly)","speed":"1.0"}]},{"id":"GV-L07-U5-LS2","title":"Someone Must Have Left the Door Open: Modals of Deduction (Past)","objectives":["Students will be able to make deductions about the past with must have, can't have and might have + past participle.","Students will be able to choose between present and past deduction.","I can say \"It must have rained last night\" when the streets are wet.","I can say \"He can't have seen the message\" and \"She might have missed the bus.\""],"objectives_ar":["سيتمكن الطلاب من الاستنتاج عن الماضي بـ must have وcan't have وmight have + التصريف الثالث.","سيتمكن الطلاب من الاختيار بين الاستنتاج عن الحاضر والاستنتاج عن الماضي.","أستطيع أن أقول It must have rained last night عندما تكون الشوارع مبتلة.","أستطيع أن أقول He can't have seen the message وShe might have missed the bus."],"vocabulary":[{"word":"skyscraper","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈskaɪˌskreɪpɚ/","definition":"a very tall building in a city","arabic":"ناطحة سحاب","example":"Dubai has some of the tallest skyscrapers in the world.","image_id":"GV-L07-U5-LS2-W01","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L07-U5-LS2-W01"},{"word":"traffic jam","pos":"noun phrase","ipa":"/ˈtræfɪk dʒæm/","definition":"a long line of cars that can't move or move very slowly","arabic":"ازدحام مروري","example":"We were stuck in a traffic jam for an hour.","image_id":"GV-L07-U5-LS2-W02","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L07-U5-LS2-W02"},{"word":"public transportation","pos":"noun phrase","ipa":"/ˈpʌblɪk ˌtrænspɚˈteɪʃən/","definition":"buses, trains and metros that everyone can use","arabic":"المواصلات العامة","example":"Public transportation reduces pollution.","image_id":"GV-L07-U5-LS2-W03","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L07-U5-LS2-W03"},{"word":"pedestrian","pos":"noun","ipa":"/pəˈdɛstriən/","definition":"a person who is walking in a street","arabic":"المشاة / راجل","example":"This street is only for pedestrians.","image_id":"GV-L07-U5-LS2-W04","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L07-U5-LS2-W04"}],"explanation":{"text":"To make a deduction about the past, use modal + have + past participle. must have = I'm sure it happened: The streets are wet. It must have rained last night.\ncan't have / couldn't have = I'm sure it didn't happen: He can't have seen the message – he hasn't replied. might have / may have / could have = it possibly happened: She might have missed the bus.\nCompare present deduction (must be) with past deduction (must have been): He must be at home now. ↔ He must have been at home yesterday. Don't forget have, and use the past participle: (not: must have went) → must have gone.\nmust have + past participle = sure it happened\ncan't have / couldn't have + past participle = sure it didn't happen\nmight / may / could have + past participle = possibly happened\nNot: must went / must have went → must have gone","examples":["The ground is white. It must have snowed in the mountains.","Faisal can't have stolen the money – he was with me all day.","The window is broken. A ball might have hit it.","Ancient people must have used this tool for cooking.","My keys aren't here. I may have left them in the car.","The cake is gone! My brothers must have eaten it.","She couldn't have walked 50 km in one day.","The workers could have finished the bridge earlier with better machines."],"common_errors":["✗ It must rained last night. → ✓ It must have rained last night. (Past deduction → must have + past participle.)","✗ He can't have went home. → ✓ He can't have gone home. (have + past participle.)","✗ She mustn't have seen me. (I'm sure she didn't) → ✓ She can't have seen me. (Negative deduction → can't have.)","✗ He must have be at school. → ✓ He must have been at school. (be → been.)"],"arabic":"للاستنتاج عن الماضي نستخدم الفعل الناقص + have + التصريف الثالث.\nmust have (متأكد أنه حدث): It must have rained last night.\ncan't have / couldn't have (متأكد أنه لم يحدث): He can't have seen the message.\nmight / may / could have (ربما حدث): She might have missed the bus."},"video":{"script":[{"time":"00:00–00:20","narration":"Hi, I’m Zaki! Today’s lesson is “Someone Must Have Left the Door Open: Modals of Deduction (Past)”. Let’s learn must have / can't have / couldn't have / might have / may have / could have + past participle for deductions about the past; contrast with present deduction together.","on_screen":"GV-L07-U5-LS2 | Someone Must Have Left the Door Open: Modals of Deduction (Past)","visual":"Zaki the Falcon flies in over the Leaf Green title card and lands next to the lesson title; soft chime."},{"time":"00:20–00:45","narration":"Remember these patterns: Someone must have left the door open. She can't have finished already. • He might not have heard you. Who could have taken my pen?","on_screen":"Someone must have left the door open. | She can't have finished already. • He might not have heard you. | Who could have taken my pen?","visual":"Pattern strips slide in from the left; the key words are highlighted in Leaf Green."},{"time":"00:45–01:30","narration":"To make a deduction about the past, use modal + have + past participle. must have = I'm sure it happened: The streets are wet. It must have rained last night. can't have / couldn't have = I'm sure it didn't happen: He can't have seen the message – he hasn't replied. might have / may have / could have = it possibly happened: She might have missed the bus.","on_screen":"must have + past participle = sure it happened • can't have / couldn't have + past participle = sure it didn't happen • might / may / could have + past participle = possibly happened","visual":"Grammar box builds line by line (form → meaning → use); Zaki points to each line."},{"time":"01:30–02:15","narration":"Here are some examples. The ground is white. It must have snowed in the mountains. Faisal can't have stolen the money – he was with me all day. The window is broken. A ball might have hit it.","on_screen":"The ground is white. It must have snowed in the mountains. / Faisal can't have stolen the money – he was with me all day. / The window is broken. A ball might have hit it.","visual":"Each example appears on a card with a small picture; the target part bounces once and turns green."},{"time":"02:15–02:45","narration":"Be careful! Some learners say: “It must rained last night.” That’s not right. We say: “It must have rained last night.” Past deduction → must have + past participle.","on_screen":"✗ It must rained last night.   ✓ It must have rained last night.","visual":"A red cross stamps the wrong sentence; it slides away and the correct sentence appears with a green tick."},{"time":"02:45–03:05","narration":"Quick check: \"It must have rained.\" Did I see the rain? … Think! … No – I see wet streets, so I'm sure it rained. Great job! Now you can say: I can say \"It must have rained last night\" when the streets are wet.","on_screen":"Quick check ✔  |  I can: I can say \"It must have rained last night\" when the streets are wet.","visual":"Three-second pause with a countdown ring; Zaki gives a wing \"thumbs up\" and confetti in the programme colours."}],"captions_ar":["مرحبًا، أنا زكي! درس اليوم: must have / can't have / couldn't have / might have / may have / could have + past participle for deductions about the past; contrast with present deduction.","استمع وانتبه إلى الكلمات الملوّنة بالأخضر.","للاستنتاج عن الماضي نستخدم الفعل الناقص + have + التصريف الثالث.","لاحظ الأمثلة: الجزء الملوّن هو القاعدة.","انتبه! الخطأ: It must rained last night. — الصحيح: It must have rained last night.","سؤال سريع… فكّر ثم أجب. أحسنت! الآن تستطيع: أستطيع أن أقول It must have rained last night عندما تكون الشوارع مبتلة."]},"texts":[],"activities":[{"id":"GV-L07-U5-LS2-A1","type":"mcq","instructions":"Controlled practice: Choose the correct answer.","items":[{"q":"The streets are wet. It ___ during the night.","options":["must have rained","can't have rained","must rain","must have rain"],"answer":"must have rained","explanation":"Sure it happened → must have + past participle.","explanation_ar":"must have."},{"q":"Faisal ___ my message. He always replies quickly, but he hasn't replied yet.","options":["can't read","can't have read","mustn't have read","must have read"],"answer":"can't have read","explanation":"Sure it didn't happen → can't have / couldn't have.","explanation_ar":"can't have."},{"q":"I'm not sure why the bus was late. There ___ an accident.","options":["must be","can't have been","might be","might have been"],"answer":"might have been","explanation":"Possibly happened → might / may / could have.","explanation_ar":"might have."},{"q":"","options":["She must have forgotten her key.","She must had forgotten her key.","She must forgotten her key.","She must have forget her key."],"answer":"She must have forgotten her key.","explanation":"have + past participle (been, gone, seen).","explanation_ar":"have + التصريف الثالث."},{"q":"The ancient city is empty now, but thousands of people ___ there long ago.","options":["can't have lived","must lived","must live","must have lived"],"answer":"must have lived","explanation":"Sure it happened → must have + past participle.","explanation_ar":"must have."},{"q":"Which sentence is a deduction about the past?","options":["He must be on the train.","He might miss the train.","He might have missed the train.","He can't be on the train."],"answer":"He might have missed the train.","explanation":"Present (must be) or past (must have been)?","explanation_ar":"الحاضر أم الماضي؟"}]},{"id":"GV-L07-U5-LS2-B1","type":"gap_fill","instructions":"Guided practice: Complete with the correct past modal. Word bank: might have left, must have kicked, can't have finished","items":[{"q":"The window is broken, and there's a ball on the floor. Someone ______ (kick) a ball through it.","options":[],"answer":"must have kicked","explanation":"Sure it happened → must have + past participle.","explanation_ar":"must have."},{"q":"Omar ______ (finish) the project already – he only started an hour ago.","options":[],"answer":"can't have finished","explanation":"Sure it didn't happen → can't have / couldn't have.","explanation_ar":"can't have."},{"q":"I'm not sure where my phone is. I ______ (leave) it in the taxi.","options":[],"answer":"might have left","explanation":"Possibly happened → might / may / could have.","explanation_ar":"might have."}]},{"id":"GV-L07-U5-LS2-B2","type":"open","instructions":"Guided practice: Rewrite with a past modal of deduction.","items":[{"q":"I'm sure the workers built this bridge quickly.  (must have)","options":[],"answer":"The workers must have built this bridge quickly.","explanation":"Sure it happened → must have + past participle.","explanation_ar":"must have."},{"q":"It's impossible that Lina saw the film – she was at home all evening.  (can't have)","options":[],"answer":"Lina can't have seen the film – she was at home all evening.","explanation":"Sure it didn't happen → can't have / couldn't have.","explanation_ar":"can't have."},{"q":"Maybe the power went off because of the storm.  (might have)","options":[],"answer":"The power might have gone off because of the storm.","explanation":"Possibly happened → might / may / could have.","explanation_ar":"might have."}]},{"id":"GV-L07-U5-LS2-C1","type":"open","instructions":"Freer practice: Solve the mysteries.","items":[{"q":"Your homework is wet, and the glass of water is empty. => ___","options":[],"answer":"Someone must have knocked over the glass.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses must have / can't have / couldn't have / might have / may have / could have + past participle for deductions about the past; contrast with present deduction correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Your friend got 100% in the test, but he didn't study. => ___","options":[],"answer":"He must have studied secretly – or the test might have been very easy!","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses must have / can't have / couldn't have / might have / may have / could have + past participle for deductions about the past; contrast with present deduction correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"The class is empty, but the board is full of notes. => ___","options":[],"answer":"The teacher must have given a lesson, and the class might have gone to the lab.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses must have / can't have / couldn't have / might have / may have / could have + past participle for deductions about the past; contrast with present deduction correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"There's sand all over your brother's shoes. => ___","options":[],"answer":"He must have been to the desert or the beach.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses must have / can't have / couldn't have / might have / may have / could have + past participle for deductions about the past; contrast with present deduction correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"The shop was closed at 4 p.m. on a Tuesday. => ___","options":[],"answer":"The owner might have gone to pray, or he could have been sick.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses must have / can't have / couldn't have / might have / may have / could have + past participle for deductions about the past; contrast with present deduction correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."}]},{"id":"GV-L07-U5-LS2-D1","type":"open","instructions":"Production: Detective report.","items":[{"q":"Write 3 clues about something strange that happened (real or imagined).","options":[],"answer":"The fridge was open. There were crumbs on the floor. The cat looked very happy.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses must have / can't have / couldn't have / might have / may have / could have + past participle for deductions about the past; contrast with present deduction correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Write 3 deductions with must have, might have and can't have.","options":[],"answer":"The cat must have opened the fridge. It might have eaten the chicken. It can't have closed the door by itself.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses must have / can't have / couldn't have / might have / may have / could have + past participle for deductions about the past; contrast with present deduction correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Write one present and one past deduction about a person in a photo.","options":[],"answer":"He must be a farmer. He must have worked hard all his life.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses must have / can't have / couldn't have / might have / may have / could have + past participle for deductions about the past; contrast with present deduction correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."}]}],"game":{"name":"Tic-Tac-Grammar","mechanic":"tic_tac_toe","rules":["Two teams: X and O. Team X chooses a square.","Using the cue, the team says a correct sentence with must have / can't have / couldn't have / might have / may have / could have + past participle for deductions about the past; contrast with present deduction (the form in brackets: +, – or ?).","If the class and teacher agree it is correct, the team marks the square.","Three squares in a row wins. Play a second round with the grid turned around."],"data":[{"cue":"the lights are off / they / be at home (can't)"},{"cue":"he's wearing a pilot's uniform / he / be a pilot (must)"},{"cue":"the road is wet / it / rain (must have)"},{"cue":"she didn't answer / she / be asleep (might)"},{"cue":"they're smiling / they / win (must have)"},{"cue":"he's calm / he / hear the news (can't have)"},{"cue":"the store is crowded / there / be a sale (might)"},{"cue":"her bag is here / Lina / be in the lab (must)"},{"cue":"the stop is full / the bus / be late (must)"}]},"exit_quiz":[{"q":"Lina is very happy today. She ___ good news yesterday.","options":["must received","must receive","must have received","can't have received"],"answer":"must have received","explanation":"Sure it happened → must have + past participle.","explanation_ar":"must have."},{"q":"That ___ Adam you saw at the mall. He's in Makkah this week.","options":["mustn't have been","must have been","can't be had","can't have been"],"answer":"can't have been","explanation":"Sure it didn't happen → can't have / couldn't have.","explanation_ar":"can't have."},{"q":"The team lost badly. The players ___ very disappointed.","options":["must have feel","can't have felt","must feel yesterday","must have felt"],"answer":"must have felt","explanation":"Sure it happened → must have + past participle.","explanation_ar":"must have."},{"q":"","options":["My brother may taken my charger.","My brother may have taken my charger.","My brother may have took my charger.","My brother may has taken my charger."],"answer":"My brother may have taken my charger.","explanation":"have + past participle (been, gone, seen).","explanation_ar":"have + التصريف الثالث."},{"q":"I can't find my glasses. I ___ them at school.","options":["can't have leave","might have left","must left","might leave yesterday"],"answer":"might have left","explanation":"Possibly happened → might / may / could have.","explanation_ar":"might have."},{"q":"","options":["The pyramids must have took years to build.","The pyramids must have take years to build.","The pyramids must have taken years to build.","The pyramids must took years to build."],"answer":"The pyramids must have taken years to build.","explanation":"have + past participle (been, gone, seen).","explanation_ar":"have + التصريف الثالث."},{"q":"He ___ the exam already. It started only ten minutes ago!","options":["can't have finished","might finish","can't finish yesterday","must have finished"],"answer":"can't have finished","explanation":"Sure it didn't happen → can't have / couldn't have.","explanation_ar":"can't have."},{"q":"The lights were off at Saad's house last night. He ___ out.","options":["must have been","must been","can't have been","must be"],"answer":"must have been","explanation":"Sure it happened → must have + past participle.","explanation_ar":"must have."},{"q":"Which sentence is about the present?","options":["He can't have eaten.","He must have been hungry.","He might have eaten.","He must be hungry."],"answer":"He must be hungry.","explanation":"Present (must be) or past (must have been)?","explanation_ar":"الحاضر أم الماضي؟"},{"q":"The road was blocked, so the ambulance ___ another way.","options":["might take yesterday","might have taken","might have took","must take"],"answer":"might have taken","explanation":"Possibly happened → might / may / could have.","explanation_ar":"might have."}],"images":[{"id":"GV-L07-U5-LS2-IMG01","prompt":"A smart-city street in the morning: wet roads, a fallen e-scooter, a delivery drone stuck in a palm tree and a broken window with a football on the floor; Noura and Adam acting as detectives with a notebook. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as teenagers aged 14–17, realistic proportions, modern school/city settings. Landscape 16:9.","alt":"A smart-city street in the morning: wet roads, a fallen e-scooter, a delivery drone stuck in a palm tree and a broken window with a football on the floor; Noura and Adam acting as detectives with a notebook"},{"id":"GV-L07-U5-LS2-IMG02","prompt":"two-panel visual contrasting correct and incorrect use of must have / can't have / couldn't have / might have / may have / could have + past participle for deductions about the past; contrast with present deduction: a green tick panel and a soft red cross panel with simple objects from the theme “Cities of the Future”; empty space for text overlay. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as teenagers aged 14–17, realistic proportions, modern school/city settings. Square 1:1.","alt":"two-panel visual contrasting correct and incorrect use of must have / can't have / couldn't have / might have / may have / could have + past participle for deductions about the past"},{"id":"GV-L07-U5-LS2-W01","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows skyscraper (a very tall building in a city); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as teenagers aged 14–17, realistic proportions, modern school/city settings. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing skyscraper: a very tall building in a city"},{"id":"GV-L07-U5-LS2-W02","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows traffic jam (a long line of cars that can't move or move very slowly); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as teenagers aged 14–17, realistic proportions, modern school/city settings. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing traffic jam: a long line of cars that can't move or move very slowly"},{"id":"GV-L07-U5-LS2-W03","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows public transportation (buses, trains and metros that everyone can use); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as teenagers aged 14–17, realistic proportions, modern school/city settings. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing public transportation: buses, trains and metros that everyone can use"},{"id":"GV-L07-U5-LS2-W04","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows pedestrian (a person who is walking in a street); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as teenagers aged 14–17, realistic proportions, modern school/city settings. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing pedestrian: a person who is walking in a street"},{"id":"GV-L07-U5-LS2-G01","prompt":"Card-back and board design for the classroom game “Tic-Tac-Grammar”: Zaki the Falcon icon in the centre, Leaf Green border with navy stars. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image. Portrait 2:3.","alt":"Game card design for Tic-Tac-Grammar"}],"audio":[{"id":"AUD-GV-L07-U5-LS2-W01","script":"skyscraper. skyscraper. Dubai has some of the tallest skyscrapers in the world.","voice":"en-US, natural young-adult voice","speed":"1.0"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L07-U5-LS2-W02","script":"traffic jam. traffic jam. We were stuck in a traffic jam for an hour.","voice":"en-US, natural young-adult voice","speed":"1.0"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L07-U5-LS2-W03","script":"public transportation. public transportation. Public transportation reduces pollution.","voice":"en-US, natural young-adult voice","speed":"1.0"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L07-U5-LS2-W04","script":"pedestrian. pedestrian. This street is only for pedestrians.","voice":"en-US, natural young-adult voice","speed":"1.0"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L07-U5-LS2-VID","script":"Hi, I’m Zaki! Today’s lesson is “Someone Must Have Left the Door Open: Modals of Deduction (Past)”. Let’s learn must have / can't have / couldn't have / might have / may have / could have + past participle for deductions about the past; contrast with present deduction together. Remember these patterns: Someone must have left the door open. She can't have finished already. • He might not have heard you. Who could have taken my pen? To make a deduction about the past, use modal + have + past participle. must have = I'm sure it happened: The streets are wet. It must have rained last night. can't have / couldn't have = I'm sure it didn't happen: He can't have seen the message – he hasn't replied. might have / may have / could have = it possibly happened: She might have missed the bus. Here are some examples. The ground is white. It must have snowed in the mountains. Faisal can't have stolen the money – he was with me all day. The window is broken. A ball might have hit it. Be careful! Some learners say: “It must rained last night.” That’s not right. We say: “It must have rained last night.” Past deduction → must have + past participle. Quick check: \"It must have rained.\" Did I see the rain? … Think! … No – I see wet streets, so I'm sure it rained. Great job! Now you can say: I can say \"It must have rained last night\" when the streets are wet.","voice":"en-US, Zaki the Falcon narrator voice (bright, friendly)","speed":"1.0"}]},{"id":"GV-L07-U5-LS3","title":"Skyscrapers, Sidewalks and Solar Panels: Urban Compound Nouns","objectives":["Students will be able to use urban compound nouns to describe cities.","Students will be able to write compound nouns correctly as one word, two words or with a hyphen.","I can describe a city with words like skyscraper, traffic jam and public transportation.","I can spell compound nouns correctly."],"objectives_ar":["سيتمكن الطلاب من استخدام الأسماء المركبة لوصف المدن.","سيتمكن الطلاب من كتابة الأسماء المركبة بشكل صحيح كلمة واحدة أو كلمتين أو بشرطة.","أستطيع أن أصف مدينة بكلمات مثل skyscraper وtraffic jam وpublic transportation.","أستطيع أن أكتب الأسماء المركبة بشكل صحيح."],"vocabulary":[{"word":"commute","pos":"verb","ipa":"/kəˈmjut/","definition":"to travel regularly between home and work or school","arabic":"يتنقّل يوميًّا","example":"My father commutes to Jeddah every day.","image_id":"GV-L07-U5-LS3-W01","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L07-U5-LS3-W01"},{"word":"pollution","pos":"noun","ipa":"/pəˈluʃən/","definition":"damage to air, water or land by harmful substances","arabic":"التلوّث","example":"Cars are a major cause of air pollution.","image_id":"GV-L07-U5-LS3-W02","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L07-U5-LS3-W02"},{"word":"solar panel","pos":"noun phrase","ipa":"/ˈsoʊlɚ ˈpænəl/","definition":"a flat panel that turns sunlight into electricity","arabic":"لوح شمسي","example":"Our school has solar panels on the roof.","image_id":"GV-L07-U5-LS3-W03","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L07-U5-LS3-W03"},{"word":"crowded","pos":"adjective","ipa":"/ˈkraʊdəd/","definition":"full of people","arabic":"مزدحم","example":"The market is very crowded before Eid.","image_id":"GV-L07-U5-LS3-W04","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L07-U5-LS3-W04"},{"word":"vertical farm","pos":"noun phrase","ipa":"/ˈvɝtɪkəl fɑrm/","definition":"a building where crops grow on many floors","arabic":"مزرعة عمودية","example":"A vertical farm uses very little water.","image_id":"GV-L07-U5-LS3-W05","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L07-U5-LS3-W05"},{"word":"smart city","pos":"noun phrase","ipa":"/smɑrt ˈsɪti/","definition":"a city that uses technology and data to work better","arabic":"مدينة ذكية","example":"In a smart city, traffic lights change with the traffic.","image_id":"GV-L07-U5-LS3-W06","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L07-U5-LS3-W06"}],"explanation":{"text":"A compound noun is made of two (or more) words that work as one noun. Some are closed (one word): skyscraper, sidewalk, crosswalk, streetlight, downtown. Some are open (two words): traffic jam, bus stop, solar panel, parking lot, rush hour, city center. Some are hyphenated: high-rise, drive-through. Check a dictionary when you aren't sure.\nIn most compound nouns, the second word is the main noun and the first word describes it: a bus stop is a kind of stop; a traffic light is a kind of light. The plural goes on the main noun: bus stops, traffic jams.\nAmerican city words: sidewalk (path for walking), parking lot (open place for cars), downtown (city center), subway / metro (underground train), crosswalk (place to cross the street), apartment (flat).\nCollocations/phrases: closed: skyscraper • sidewalk • crosswalk • streetlight • downtown • rooftop | open: traffic jam • bus stop • parking lot • rush hour • solar panel • bike lane | open: public transportation • power station • green space • metro station • smart city | hyphenated: high-rise • drive-through • self-driving car","examples":["The city is full of skyscrapers.","We waited at the bus stop for ten minutes.","Never cross the road outside the crosswalk.","There's always a traffic jam at rush hour.","My uncle commutes to downtown Riyadh by metro.","Cities need more green spaces for children to play.","Air pollution is a serious problem in crowded cities.","Self-driving cars might be common in the future."],"common_errors":["✗ There are many sky scrapers in Dubai. → ✓ There are many skyscrapers in Dubai. (Closed compound → one word.)","✗ We were stuck in a jam traffic. → ✓ We were stuck in a traffic jam. (The main noun comes second.)","✗ There are two buses stop on my street. → ✓ There are two bus stops on my street. (Plural on the main noun.)","✗ Walk on the side walk. → ✓ Walk on the sidewalk. (One word.)"],"arabic":"الاسم المركب كلمتان أو أكثر تعملان كاسم واحد، وقد يُكتب كلمة واحدة (skyscraper) أو كلمتين (traffic jam) أو بشرطة (high-rise).\nالكلمة الثانية هي الاسم الأساسي، والأولى تصفه: bus stop نوع من المواقف.\nالجمع يكون على الكلمة الأساسية: bus stops وtraffic jams.\nكلمات أمريكية: sidewalk (الرصيف) وparking lot (موقف السيارات) وdowntown (وسط المدينة) وcrosswalk (ممر المشاة)."},"video":{"script":[{"time":"00:00–00:20","narration":"Hi, I’m Zaki! Today’s lesson is “Skyscrapers, Sidewalks and Solar Panels: Urban Compound Nouns”. Let’s learn compound nouns for city life (closed: skyscraper, sidewalk; open: traffic jam, solar panel; hyphenated: high-rise); city vocabulary; American city words together.","on_screen":"GV-L07-U5-LS3 | Skyscrapers, Sidewalks and Solar Panels: Urban Compound Nouns","visual":"Zaki the Falcon flies in over the Leaf Green title card and lands next to the lesson title; soft chime."},{"time":"00:20–00:45","narration":"Meet some new words. commute: to travel regularly between home and work or school. pollution: damage to air, water or land by harmful substances. solar panel: a flat panel that turns sunlight into electricity.","on_screen":"commute | pollution | solar panel","visual":"Each word card flips over to show its picture (vocabulary image briefs) and Arabic meaning."},{"time":"00:45–01:30","narration":"A compound noun is made of two (or more) words that work as one noun. Some are closed (one word): skyscraper, sidewalk, crosswalk, streetlight, downtown. Some are open (two words): traffic jam, bus stop, solar panel, parking lot, rush hour, city center. Some are hyphenated: high-rise, drive-through. Check a dictionary when you aren't sure. In most compound nouns, the second word is the main noun and the first word describes it: a bus stop is a kind of stop; a traffic light is a kind of light. The plural goes on the main noun: bus stops, traffic jams.","on_screen":"compound nouns for city life (closed: skyscraper, sidewalk; open: traffic jam, solar panel; hyphenated: high-rise); city vocabulary; American city words","visual":"Grammar box builds line by line (form → meaning → use); Zaki points to each line."},{"time":"01:30–02:15","narration":"Here are some examples. The city is full of skyscrapers. We waited at the bus stop for ten minutes. Never cross the road outside the crosswalk.","on_screen":"The city is full of skyscrapers. / We waited at the bus stop for ten minutes. / Never cross the road outside the crosswalk.","visual":"Each example appears on a card with a small picture; the target part bounces once and turns green."},{"time":"02:15–02:45","narration":"Be careful! Some learners say: “There are many sky scrapers in Dubai.” That’s not right. We say: “There are many skyscrapers in Dubai.” Closed compound → one word.","on_screen":"✗ There are many sky scrapers in Dubai.   ✓ There are many skyscrapers in Dubai.","visual":"A red cross stamps the wrong sentence; it slides away and the correct sentence appears with a green tick."},{"time":"02:45–03:05","narration":"Quick check: Is a \"bus stop\" a kind of bus or a kind of stop? … Think! … A kind of stop. Great job! Now you can say: I can describe a city with words like skyscraper, traffic jam and public transportation.","on_screen":"Quick check ✔  |  I can: I can describe a city with words like skyscraper, traffic jam and public transportation.","visual":"Three-second pause with a countdown ring; Zaki gives a wing \"thumbs up\" and confetti in the programme colours."}],"captions_ar":["مرحبًا، أنا زكي! درس اليوم: compound nouns for city life (closed: skyscraper, sidewalk; open: traffic jam, solar panel; hyphenated: high-rise); city vocabulary; American city words.","استمع وانتبه إلى الكلمات الملوّنة بالأخضر.","الاسم المركب كلمتان أو أكثر تعملان كاسم واحد، وقد يُكتب كلمة واحدة (skyscraper) أو كلمتين (traffic jam) أو بشرطة (high-rise).","لاحظ الأمثلة: الجزء الملوّن هو القاعدة.","انتبه! الخطأ: There are many sky scrapers in Dubai. — الصحيح: There are many skyscrapers in Dubai.","سؤال سريع… فكّر ثم أجب. أحسنت! الآن تستطيع: أستطيع أن أصف مدينة بكلمات مثل skyscraper وtraffic jam وpublic transportation."]},"texts":[],"activities":[{"id":"GV-L07-U5-LS3-A1","type":"mcq","instructions":"Controlled practice: Choose the correct word.","items":[{"q":"Thousands of people live in this city. It has a large ___.","options":["population","infrastructure","pedestrian","pollution"],"answer":"population","explanation":"Choose the city word with the right meaning.","explanation_ar":"المعنى."},{"q":"It took us an hour to drive five kilometers because of a terrible traffic ___.","options":["line","stop","block","jam"],"answer":"jam","explanation":"Choose the right compound noun.","explanation_ar":"الاسم المركب الصحيح."},{"q":"Many people go to work by metro and bus. The city has good public ___.","options":["transporting","transporter","transported","transportation"],"answer":"transportation","explanation":"Choose the right compound noun.","explanation_ar":"الاسم المركب الصحيح."},{"q":"A very tall building in a city is a ___.","options":["parking lot","crosswalk","skyscraper","sidewalk"],"answer":"skyscraper","explanation":"Choose the right compound noun.","explanation_ar":"الاسم المركب الصحيح."},{"q":"Air ___ from cars makes it hard to breathe.","options":["commute","pollution","population","pedestrian"],"answer":"pollution","explanation":"Choose the city word with the right meaning.","explanation_ar":"المعنى."},{"q":"Which compound noun is written as one word?","options":["traffic jam","bus stop","skyscraper","solar panel"],"answer":"skyscraper","explanation":"One word, two words or a hyphen?","explanation_ar":"كلمة أم كلمتان أم شرطة؟"}]},{"id":"GV-L07-U5-LS3-B1","type":"match","instructions":"Guided practice: Match the word to its meaning.","items":[{"q":"commute","options":["the busy time when people go to or from work","a marked place where people can cross the road","the path for walking at the side of a street","a person who is walking in the street","roads, bridges, pipes and power lines that a city needs","travel between home and work every day"],"answer":"travel between home and work every day","explanation":"commute → travel between home and work every day. Choose the right compound noun.","explanation_ar":"الاسم المركب الصحيح."},{"q":"pedestrian","options":["the busy time when people go to or from work","a marked place where people can cross the road","the path for walking at the side of a street","a person who is walking in the street","roads, bridges, pipes and power lines that a city needs","travel between home and work every day"],"answer":"a person who is walking in the street","explanation":"pedestrian → a person who is walking in the street. Choose the right compound noun.","explanation_ar":"الاسم المركب الصحيح."},{"q":"crosswalk","options":["the busy time when people go to or from work","a marked place where people can cross the road","the path for walking at the side of a street","a person who is walking in the street","roads, bridges, pipes and power lines that a city needs","travel between home and work every day"],"answer":"a marked place where people can cross the road","explanation":"crosswalk → a marked place where people can cross the road. Choose the right compound noun.","explanation_ar":"الاسم المركب الصحيح."},{"q":"sidewalk","options":["the busy time when people go to or from work","a marked place where people can cross the road","the path for walking at the side of a street","a person who is walking in the street","roads, bridges, pipes and power lines that a city needs","travel between home and work every day"],"answer":"the path for walking at the side of a street","explanation":"sidewalk → the path for walking at the side of a street. Choose the right compound noun.","explanation_ar":"الاسم المركب الصحيح."},{"q":"rush hour","options":["the busy time when people go to or from work","a marked place where people can cross the road","the path for walking at the side of a street","a person who is walking in the street","roads, bridges, pipes and power lines that a city needs","travel between home and work every day"],"answer":"the busy time when people go to or from work","explanation":"rush hour → the busy time when people go to or from work. Choose the right compound noun.","explanation_ar":"الاسم المركب الصحيح."},{"q":"infrastructure","options":["the busy time when people go to or from work","a marked place where people can cross the road","the path for walking at the side of a street","a person who is walking in the street","roads, bridges, pipes and power lines that a city needs","travel between home and work every day"],"answer":"roads, bridges, pipes and power lines that a city needs","explanation":"infrastructure → roads, bridges, pipes and power lines that a city needs. Choose the right compound noun.","explanation_ar":"الاسم المركب الصحيح."}]},{"id":"GV-L07-U5-LS3-C1","type":"open","instructions":"Freer practice: Describe your city.","items":[{"q":"How do you get to school? Use one compound noun.","options":[],"answer":"I take the school bus from the bus stop near my house.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses compound nouns for city life (closed: skyscraper, sidewalk; open: traffic jam, solar panel; hyphenated: high-rise); city vocabulary; American city words correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Describe the traffic in your city at rush hour.","options":[],"answer":"At rush hour, there are long traffic jams on the main road.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses compound nouns for city life (closed: skyscraper, sidewalk; open: traffic jam, solar panel; hyphenated: high-rise); city vocabulary; American city words correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"What does your city need more of?","options":[],"answer":"My city needs more green spaces and bike lanes.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses compound nouns for city life (closed: skyscraper, sidewalk; open: traffic jam, solar panel; hyphenated: high-rise); city vocabulary; American city words correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Write a sentence with \"sustainable\".","options":[],"answer":"Solar energy is a sustainable way to power our homes.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses compound nouns for city life (closed: skyscraper, sidewalk; open: traffic jam, solar panel; hyphenated: high-rise); city vocabulary; American city words correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Write a sentence with \"crowded\".","options":[],"answer":"The souq is crowded on Thursday evenings.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses compound nouns for city life (closed: skyscraper, sidewalk; open: traffic jam, solar panel; hyphenated: high-rise); city vocabulary; American city words correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."}]},{"id":"GV-L07-U5-LS3-D1","type":"open","instructions":"Production: Design a smart city.","items":[{"q":"Write 3 sentences about transportation in your smart city, using 3 compound nouns.","options":[],"answer":"There will be self-driving cars. Every street will have a bike lane. The metro stations will be air-conditioned.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses compound nouns for city life (closed: skyscraper, sidewalk; open: traffic jam, solar panel; hyphenated: high-rise); city vocabulary; American city words correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Write 2 sentences about energy and food.","options":[],"answer":"All the rooftops will have solar panels. Vertical farms will grow vegetables near people's homes.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses compound nouns for city life (closed: skyscraper, sidewalk; open: traffic jam, solar panel; hyphenated: high-rise); city vocabulary; American city words correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Write one sentence explaining why your city will be sustainable.","options":[],"answer":"It will be sustainable because it will use clean energy and recycle water.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses compound nouns for city life (closed: skyscraper, sidewalk; open: traffic jam, solar panel; hyphenated: high-rise); city vocabulary; American city words correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."}]}],"game":{"name":"Memory Match","mechanic":"matching","rules":["Place all cards face down in a grid.","Turn over two cards. If the word matches its definition, keep the pair and say a sentence with the word.","If not, turn them back over; the next player plays.","The player with the most pairs wins."],"data":[{"word":"urban","match":"connected with towns and cities","arabic":"حضري / مدني"},{"word":"population","match":"the number of people who live in a place","arabic":"عدد السكان"},{"word":"infrastructure","match":"the basic systems a city needs, such as roads, bridges, water and power","arabic":"البنية التحتية"},{"word":"sustainable","match":"able to continue without harming the environment","arabic":"مستدام"},{"word":"skyscraper","match":"a very tall building in a city","arabic":"ناطحة سحاب"},{"word":"traffic jam","match":"a long line of cars that can't move or move very slowly","arabic":"ازدحام مروري"},{"word":"public transportation","match":"buses, trains and metros that everyone can use","arabic":"المواصلات العامة"},{"word":"pedestrian","match":"a person who is walking in a street","arabic":"المشاة / راجل"},{"word":"commute","match":"to travel regularly between home and work or school","arabic":"يتنقّل يوميًّا"},{"word":"pollution","match":"damage to air, water or land by harmful substances","arabic":"التلوّث"},{"word":"solar panel","match":"a flat panel that turns sunlight into electricity","arabic":"لوح شمسي"},{"word":"crowded","match":"full of people","arabic":"مزدحم"},{"word":"vertical farm","match":"a building where crops grow on many floors","arabic":"مزرعة عمودية"},{"word":"smart city","match":"a city that uses technology and data to work better","arabic":"مدينة ذكية"}]},"exit_quiz":[{"q":"Please walk on the ___, not in the road.","options":["sidewalk","streetlight","parking lot","skyscraper"],"answer":"sidewalk","explanation":"Choose the right compound noun.","explanation_ar":"الاسم المركب الصحيح."},{"q":"There are no spaces left in the ___. We'll have to park on the street.","options":["crosswalk","rooftop","bike lane","parking lot"],"answer":"parking lot","explanation":"Choose the right compound noun.","explanation_ar":"الاسم المركب الصحيح."},{"q":"My father ___ to work by metro every day.","options":["pollutes","commutes","populates","crowds"],"answer":"commutes","explanation":"Choose the city word with the right meaning.","explanation_ar":"المعنى."},{"q":"The ___ turn on automatically when it gets dark.","options":["streetlights","crosswalks","sidewalks","skyscrapers"],"answer":"streetlights","explanation":"Choose the right compound noun.","explanation_ar":"الاسم المركب الصحيح."},{"q":"","options":["There are three bus stops on my street.","There are three buses stops on my street.","There are three bus stop on my street.","There are three buses stop on my street."],"answer":"There are three bus stops on my street.","explanation":"The plural goes on the main noun.","explanation_ar":"الجمع على الاسم الأساسي."},{"q":"Roads, bridges and water pipes are part of a city's ___.","options":["pedestrian","population","infrastructure","commute"],"answer":"infrastructure","explanation":"Choose the city word with the right meaning.","explanation_ar":"المعنى."},{"q":"Which word is hyphenated?","options":["traffic-jam","sky-scraper","side-walk","high-rise"],"answer":"high-rise","explanation":"One word, two words or a hyphen?","explanation_ar":"كلمة أم كلمتان أم شرطة؟"},{"q":"The new mall is very ___ on weekends; you can hardly move.","options":["urban","crowded","sustainable","vertical"],"answer":"crowded","explanation":"Choose the city word with the right meaning.","explanation_ar":"المعنى."},{"q":"Using wind and solar power is more ___ than burning oil.","options":["crowded","urban","sustainable","vertical"],"answer":"sustainable","explanation":"Choose the city word with the right meaning.","explanation_ar":"المعنى."},{"q":"Many ___ were waiting to cross at the traffic light.","options":["commutes","pedestrians","infrastructures","populations"],"answer":"pedestrians","explanation":"Choose the city word with the right meaning.","explanation_ar":"المعنى."}],"images":[{"id":"GV-L07-U5-LS3-IMG01","prompt":"A labeled poster of a future city street: skyscrapers, a sidewalk, a crosswalk, a bike lane, a bus stop, a metro station, streetlights, solar panels on roofs, a vertical farm and a green park; a busy traffic jam in an old city on the left for contrast. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as teenagers aged 14–17, realistic proportions, modern school/city settings. Landscape 16:9.","alt":"A labeled poster of a future city street: skyscrapers, a sidewalk, a crosswalk, a bike lane, a bus stop, a metro station, streetlights, solar panels on roofs, a vertical farm and a green park; a busy traffic jam in an old city on the left for contrast"},{"id":"GV-L07-U5-LS3-IMG02","prompt":"word-web visual: a central circle with branches to 6 small picture icons of the lesson words; empty labels. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as teenagers aged 14–17, realistic proportions, modern school/city settings. Square 1:1.","alt":"word-web visual: a central circle with branches to 6 small picture icons of the lesson words"},{"id":"GV-L07-U5-LS3-W01","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows commute (to travel regularly between home and work or school); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as teenagers aged 14–17, realistic proportions, modern school/city settings. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing commute: to travel regularly between home and work or school"},{"id":"GV-L07-U5-LS3-W02","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows pollution (damage to air, water or land by harmful substances); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as teenagers aged 14–17, realistic proportions, modern school/city settings. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing pollution: damage to air, water or land by harmful substances"},{"id":"GV-L07-U5-LS3-W03","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows solar panel (a flat panel that turns sunlight into electricity); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as teenagers aged 14–17, realistic proportions, modern school/city settings. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing solar panel: a flat panel that turns sunlight into electricity"},{"id":"GV-L07-U5-LS3-W04","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows crowded (full of people); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as teenagers aged 14–17, realistic proportions, modern school/city settings. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing crowded: full of people"},{"id":"GV-L07-U5-LS3-W05","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows vertical farm (a building where crops grow on many floors); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as teenagers aged 14–17, realistic proportions, modern school/city settings. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing vertical farm: a building where crops grow on many floors"},{"id":"GV-L07-U5-LS3-W06","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows smart city (a city that uses technology and data to work better); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as teenagers aged 14–17, realistic proportions, modern school/city settings. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing smart city: a city that uses technology and data to work better"},{"id":"GV-L07-U5-LS3-G01","prompt":"Card-back and board design for the classroom game “Memory Match”: Zaki the Falcon icon in the centre, Leaf Green border with navy stars. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image. Portrait 2:3.","alt":"Game card design for Memory Match"}],"audio":[{"id":"AUD-GV-L07-U5-LS3-W01","script":"commute. commute. My father commutes to Jeddah every day.","voice":"en-US, natural young-adult voice","speed":"1.0"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L07-U5-LS3-W02","script":"pollution. pollution. Cars are a major cause of air pollution.","voice":"en-US, natural young-adult voice","speed":"1.0"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L07-U5-LS3-W03","script":"solar panel. solar panel. Our school has solar panels on the roof.","voice":"en-US, natural young-adult voice","speed":"1.0"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L07-U5-LS3-W04","script":"crowded. crowded. The market is very crowded before Eid.","voice":"en-US, natural young-adult voice","speed":"1.0"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L07-U5-LS3-W05","script":"vertical farm. vertical farm. A vertical farm uses very little water.","voice":"en-US, natural young-adult voice","speed":"1.0"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L07-U5-LS3-W06","script":"smart city. smart city. In a smart city, traffic lights change with the traffic.","voice":"en-US, natural young-adult voice","speed":"1.0"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L07-U5-LS3-VID","script":"Hi, I’m Zaki! Today’s lesson is “Skyscrapers, Sidewalks and Solar Panels: Urban Compound Nouns”. Let’s learn compound nouns for city life (closed: skyscraper, sidewalk; open: traffic jam, solar panel; hyphenated: high-rise); city vocabulary; American city words together. Meet some new words. commute: to travel regularly between home and work or school. pollution: damage to air, water or land by harmful substances. solar panel: a flat panel that turns sunlight into electricity. A compound noun is made of two (or more) words that work as one noun. Some are closed (one word): skyscraper, sidewalk, crosswalk, streetlight, downtown. Some are open (two words): traffic jam, bus stop, solar panel, parking lot, rush hour, city center. Some are hyphenated: high-rise, drive-through. Check a dictionary when you aren't sure. In most compound nouns, the second word is the main noun and the first word describes it: a bus stop is a kind of stop; a traffic light is a kind of light. The plural goes on the main noun: bus stops, traffic jams. Here are some examples. The city is full of skyscrapers. We waited at the bus stop for ten minutes. Never cross the road outside the crosswalk. Be careful! Some learners say: “There are many sky scrapers in Dubai.” That’s not right. We say: “There are many skyscrapers in Dubai.” Closed compound → one word. Quick check: Is a \"bus stop\" a kind of bus or a kind of stop? … Think! … A kind of stop. Great job! Now you can say: I can describe a city with words like skyscraper, traffic jam and public transportation.","voice":"en-US, Zaki the Falcon narrator voice (bright, friendly)","speed":"1.0"}]},{"id":"GV-L07-U5-LS4","title":"Simple, Compound, Complex: Writing with Sentence Variety","objectives":["Students will be able to identify simple, compound, complex and compound-complex sentences.","Students will be able to combine short sentences to create variety and flow.","I can name the four types of sentences.","I can combine short sentences into longer, smoother ones."],"objectives_ar":["سيتمكن الطلاب من التعرف على الجمل البسيطة والمركبة والمعقدة والمركبة المعقدة.","سيتمكن الطلاب من دمج الجمل القصيرة لإيجاد التنوّع والانسيابية.","أستطيع أن أسمّي الأنواع الأربعة للجمل.","أستطيع أن أدمج الجمل القصيرة في جمل أطول وأكثر انسيابية."],"vocabulary":[{"word":"urban","pos":"adjective","ipa":"/ˈɝbən/","definition":"connected with towns and cities","arabic":"حضري / مدني","example":"Urban areas are growing quickly.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"population","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˌpɑpjəˈleɪʃən/","definition":"the number of people who live in a place","arabic":"عدد السكان","example":"The population of Riyadh is more than seven million.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"infrastructure","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˌɪnfrəˈstrʌktʃɚ/","definition":"the basic systems a city needs, such as roads, bridges, water and power","arabic":"البنية التحتية","example":"Good infrastructure makes life easier.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"sustainable","pos":"adjective","ipa":"/səˈsteɪnəbəl/","definition":"able to continue without harming the environment","arabic":"مستدام","example":"We need sustainable sources of energy.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"skyscraper","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈskaɪˌskreɪpɚ/","definition":"a very tall building in a city","arabic":"ناطحة سحاب","example":"Dubai has some of the tallest skyscrapers in the world.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"traffic jam","pos":"noun phrase","ipa":"/ˈtræfɪk dʒæm/","definition":"a long line of cars that can't move or move very slowly","arabic":"ازدحام مروري","example":"We were stuck in a traffic jam for an hour.","image_id":"","audio_id":""}],"explanation":{"text":"A simple sentence has one independent clause (subject + verb): The metro is fast. A compound sentence joins two independent clauses with a comma + for, and, nor, but, or, yet, so (FANBOYS) or with a semicolon: The metro is fast, but it is crowded.\nA complex sentence has one independent clause and at least one dependent clause (with because, although, when, if, while, after, which, who…): Because the metro is fast, many people use it. A compound-complex sentence has two independent clauses and at least one dependent clause: Although the city is big, the metro is fast, and the buses are clean.\nGood writers mix sentence types and vary the beginnings (start with a time phrase, an -ing phrase or a dependent clause). Too many short simple sentences sound choppy; too many long sentences are hard to follow.\nsimple = 1 independent clause\ncompound = 2 independent clauses + , FANBOYS or ;\ncomplex = 1 independent + 1 dependent clause\ncompound-complex = 2 independent + 1 dependent clause","examples":["Solar panels cover the roofs. (simple)","The bike lanes are safe, so many students cycle to school. (compound)","The streets are quiet; most people use the metro. (compound)","When the sun sets, the streetlights turn on automatically. (complex)","The city, which was built in the desert, uses very little water. (complex)","Although it was rush hour, the roads were empty, and the air was clean. (compound-complex)","Riyadh's new metro, which has six lines, connects many neighborhoods. (complex)","People walk or cycle, and the air is clean because there are few cars. (compound-complex)"],"common_errors":["✗ The city is growing, it needs more schools. → ✓ The city is growing, so it needs more schools. (Two independent clauses → comma + FANBOYS (not just a comma).)","✗ Because the city is crowded. → ✓ Because the city is crowded, the government built a metro. (A dependent clause can't stand alone.)","✗ The city has a park. It has a lake. It has a museum. → ✓ The city has a park with a lake, and it also has a museum. (Combine choppy sentences.)","✗ Although it was late, but the shops were open. → ✓ Although it was late, the shops were open. (Don't use although and but together.)"],"arabic":"الجملة البسيطة فيها جملة مستقلة واحدة، والمركبة جملتان مستقلتان بفاصلة وأداة ربط (FANBOYS) أو فاصلة منقوطة.\nالجملة المعقدة فيها جملة مستقلة وجملة تابعة (because / although / when / which)، والمركبة المعقدة فيها جملتان مستقلتان وجملة تابعة.\nنوّع أنواع الجمل وبداياتها؛ الجمل القصيرة الكثيرة تبدو متقطعة.\nخطأ شائع عند العرب: Although … but معًا، والصحيح استخدام واحدة فقط."},"video":{"script":[{"time":"00:00–00:20","narration":"Hi, I’m Zaki! Today’s lesson is “Simple, Compound, Complex: Writing with Sentence Variety”. Let’s learn four sentence types: simple, compound (FANBOYS / semicolon), complex (subordinating conjunctions and relative pronouns), compound-complex; combining choppy sentences; varying sentence openings together.","on_screen":"GV-L07-U5-LS4 | Simple, Compound, Complex: Writing with Sentence Variety","visual":"Zaki the Falcon flies in over the Leaf Green title card and lands next to the lesson title; soft chime."},{"time":"00:20–00:45","narration":"A simple sentence has one independent clause (subject + verb): The metro is fast. A compound sentence joins two independent clauses with a comma + for, and, nor, but, or, yet, so (FANBOYS) or with a semicolon: The metro is fast, but it is crowded.","on_screen":"four sentence types: simple, compound (FANBOYS / semicolon), complex (subordinating conjunctions and relative pronouns), compound-complex; combining choppy sentences; varying sentence openings","visual":"Pattern strips slide in from the left; the key words are highlighted in Leaf Green."},{"time":"00:45–01:30","narration":"A simple sentence has one independent clause (subject + verb): The metro is fast. A compound sentence joins two independent clauses with a comma + for, and, nor, but, or, yet, so (FANBOYS) or with a semicolon: The metro is fast, but it is crowded. A complex sentence has one independent clause and at least one dependent clause (with because, although, when, if, while, after, which, who…): Because the metro is fast, many people use it. A compound-complex sentence has two independent clauses and at least one dependent clause: Although the city is big, the metro is fast, and the buses are clean.","on_screen":"simple = 1 independent clause • compound = 2 independent clauses + , FANBOYS or ; • complex = 1 independent + 1 dependent clause","visual":"Grammar box builds line by line (form → meaning → use); Zaki points to each line."},{"time":"01:30–02:15","narration":"Here are some examples. Solar panels cover the roofs. (simple) The bike lanes are safe, so many students cycle to school. (compound) The streets are quiet; most people use the metro. (compound)","on_screen":"Solar panels cover the roofs. (simple) / The bike lanes are safe, so many students cycle to school. (compound) / The streets are quiet; most people use the metro. (compound)","visual":"Each example appears on a card with a small picture; the target part bounces once and turns green."},{"time":"02:15–02:45","narration":"Be careful! Some learners say: “The city is growing, it needs more schools.” That’s not right. We say: “The city is growing, so it needs more schools.” Two independent clauses → comma + FANBOYS (not just a comma).","on_screen":"✗ The city is growing, it needs more schools.   ✓ The city is growing, so it needs more schools.","visual":"A red cross stamps the wrong sentence; it slides away and the correct sentence appears with a green tick."},{"time":"02:45–03:05","narration":"Quick check: \"When it rains, the streets flood.\" How many clauses? Which is dependent? … Think! … Two – \"When it rains\" is dependent. Great job! Now you can say: I can name the four types of sentences.","on_screen":"Quick check ✔  |  I can: I can name the four types of sentences.","visual":"Three-second pause with a countdown ring; Zaki gives a wing \"thumbs up\" and confetti in the programme colours."}],"captions_ar":["مرحبًا، أنا زكي! درس اليوم: four sentence types: simple, compound (FANBOYS / semicolon), complex (subordinating conjunctions and relative pronouns), compound-complex; combining choppy sentences; varying sentence openings.","استمع وانتبه إلى الكلمات الملوّنة بالأخضر.","الجملة البسيطة فيها جملة مستقلة واحدة، والمركبة جملتان مستقلتان بفاصلة وأداة ربط (FANBOYS) أو فاصلة منقوطة.","لاحظ الأمثلة: الجزء الملوّن هو القاعدة.","انتبه! الخطأ: The city is growing, it needs more schools. — الصحيح: The city is growing, so it needs more schools.","سؤال سريع… فكّر ثم أجب. أحسنت! الآن تستطيع: أستطيع أن أسمّي الأنواع الأربعة للجمل."]},"texts":[{"type":"reading","title":"Our Future Neighborhood (editing passage)","body":"Our neighborhood will have a park. It will have a lake. Cars will not be allowed, people will walk or cycle. The houses will have solar panels. They will save energy. There will be a market. There will be a library. Because the streets will be quiet. Everyone will love living there.","word_count":52,"audio_id":""}],"activities":[{"id":"GV-L07-U5-LS4-A1","type":"mcq","instructions":"Controlled practice: Choose the correct answer.","items":[{"q":"What type of sentence is \"The metro is fast and cheap.\"?","options":["simple","compound","complex","compound-complex"],"answer":"simple","explanation":"Simple sentence: one independent clause.","explanation_ar":"الجملة البسيطة."},{"q":"What type of sentence is \"The metro is fast, but it is often crowded.\"?","options":["compound-complex","complex","compound","simple"],"answer":"compound","explanation":"Compound sentence: two independent clauses + , FANBOYS or ;.","explanation_ar":"الجملة المركبة."},{"q":"What type of sentence is \"Because the metro is fast, many people use it.\"?","options":["compound","complex","compound-complex","simple"],"answer":"complex","explanation":"Complex sentence: independent + dependent clause.","explanation_ar":"الجملة المعقدة."},{"q":"What type of sentence is \"Although the city is big, the metro is fast, and the buses are clean.\"?","options":["complex","simple","compound","compound-complex"],"answer":"compound-complex","explanation":"Compound-complex: two independent + one dependent clause.","explanation_ar":"المركبة المعقدة."},{"q":"","options":["The city is growing quickly so, it needs more schools.","The city is growing quickly it needs more schools.","The city is growing quickly, so it needs more schools.","The city is growing quickly, it needs more schools."],"answer":"The city is growing quickly, so it needs more schools.","explanation":"Compound sentence: two independent clauses + , FANBOYS or ;.","explanation_ar":"الجملة المركبة."},{"q":"Which sentence combines the ideas best? \"Riyadh has a new metro. It has six lines. It connects many neighborhoods.\"","options":["Riyadh has a new metro, it has six lines, it connects many neighborhoods.","Riyadh's new metro, which has six lines, connects many neighborhoods.","Riyadh has a new metro. Has six lines. Connects many neighborhoods.","Riyadh has a new metro and it has six lines and it connects many neighborhoods."],"answer":"Riyadh's new metro, which has six lines, connects many neighborhoods.","explanation":"Combine choppy sentences smoothly.","explanation_ar":"دمج الجمل."}]},{"id":"GV-L07-U5-LS4-B1","type":"gap_fill","instructions":"Guided practice: Write the type: simple, compound, complex or compound-complex. Word bank: simple, compound-complex, complex","items":[{"q":"Solar panels cover the roofs of every house. → ______","options":[],"answer":"simple","explanation":"Simple sentence: one independent clause.","explanation_ar":"الجملة البسيطة."},{"q":"When the sun sets, the streetlights turn on by themselves. → ______","options":[],"answer":"complex","explanation":"Complex sentence: independent + dependent clause.","explanation_ar":"الجملة المعقدة."},{"q":"People walk or cycle everywhere, and the air is clean because there are very few cars. → ______","options":[],"answer":"compound-complex","explanation":"Compound-complex: two independent + one dependent clause.","explanation_ar":"المركبة المعقدة."}]},{"id":"GV-L07-U5-LS4-B2","type":"open","instructions":"Guided practice: Combine the sentences to make the type in brackets.","items":[{"q":"The bike lanes are safe.  +  Many students cycle to school. (compound: so)","options":[],"answer":"The bike lanes are safe, so many students cycle to school.","explanation":"Compound sentence: two independent clauses + , FANBOYS or ;.","explanation_ar":"الجملة المركبة."},{"q":"It was rush hour.  +  The roads were empty. (complex: although)","options":[],"answer":"Although it was rush hour, the roads were empty.","explanation":"Complex sentence: independent + dependent clause.","explanation_ar":"الجملة المعقدة."},{"q":"The metro is clean.  +  People leave their cars at home.  +  The city has less pollution. (compound-complex: because, and)","options":[],"answer":"People leave their cars at home because the metro is clean, and the city has less pollution.","explanation":"Compound-complex: two independent + one dependent clause.","explanation_ar":"المركبة المعقدة."}]},{"id":"GV-L07-U5-LS4-C1","type":"open","instructions":"Freer practice: Edit the paragraph for sentence variety.","items":[{"q":"Our neighborhood will have a park. It will have a lake.","options":[],"answer":"Our neighborhood will have a park with a lake.","explanation":"Our neighborhood will have a park. It will have a lake. → Our neighborhood will have a park with a lake.. Simple sentence: one independent clause.","explanation_ar":"التصحيح: Our neighborhood will have a park. It will have a lake. → Our neighborhood will have a park with a lake.. الجملة البسيطة."},{"q":"It will have a lake.->Our neighborhood will have a park with a lake.] Cars will not be allowed, people will walk or cycle. [The houses will have solar panels.","options":[],"answer":"It will have a lake.->Our neighborhood will have a park with a lake.] Cars will not be allowed, so people will walk or cycle. [The houses will have solar panels.","explanation":"Cars will not be allowed, people will walk or cycle. → Cars will not be allowed, so people will walk or cycle.. Simple sentence: one independent clause.","explanation_ar":"التصحيح: Cars will not be allowed, people will walk or cycle. → Cars will not be allowed, so people will walk or cycle.. الجملة البسيطة."},{"q":"The houses will have solar panels. They will save energy.","options":[],"answer":"The houses will have solar panels, which will save energy.","explanation":"The houses will have solar panels. They will save energy. → The houses will have solar panels, which will save energy.. Simple sentence: one independent clause.","explanation_ar":"التصحيح: The houses will have solar panels. They will save energy. → The houses will have solar panels, which will save energy.. الجملة البسيطة."},{"q":"There will be a market. There will be a library.","options":[],"answer":"There will be a market and a library.","explanation":"There will be a market. There will be a library. → There will be a market and a library.. Simple sentence: one independent clause.","explanation_ar":"التصحيح: There will be a market. There will be a library. → There will be a market and a library.. الجملة البسيطة."},{"q":"There will be a library.->There will be a market and a library.] Because the streets will be quiet. Everyone will love living there.","options":[],"answer":"There will be a library.->There will be a market and a library.] Because the streets will be quiet, children will play outside safely. Everyone will love living there.","explanation":"Because the streets will be quiet. → Because the streets will be quiet, children will play outside safely.. Simple sentence: one independent clause.","explanation_ar":"التصحيح: Because the streets will be quiet. → Because the streets will be quiet, children will play outside safely.. الجملة البسيطة."}]},{"id":"GV-L07-U5-LS4-D1","type":"open","instructions":"Production: Write with variety.","items":[{"q":"Write one simple and one compound sentence about your street.","options":[],"answer":"My street is narrow. It has old houses, but the people are very friendly.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses four sentence types: simple, compound (FANBOYS / semicolon), complex (subordinating conjunctions and relative pronouns), compound-complex; combining choppy sentences; varying sentence openings correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Write one complex sentence that starts with a dependent clause.","options":[],"answer":"When the weather is cool, families sit outside in the evening.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses four sentence types: simple, compound (FANBOYS / semicolon), complex (subordinating conjunctions and relative pronouns), compound-complex; combining choppy sentences; varying sentence openings correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Write one compound-complex sentence about a city you want to visit.","options":[],"answer":"I want to visit Tokyo because the trains are amazing, and I'd love to see the cherry blossoms.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses four sentence types: simple, compound (FANBOYS / semicolon), complex (subordinating conjunctions and relative pronouns), compound-complex; combining choppy sentences; varying sentence openings correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."}]}],"game":{"name":"Word Builder","mechanic":"word_builder","rules":["The teacher reads a word and a short clue.","Teams build the word with letter tiles in 30 seconds.","The team holds up the word; correct spelling = 1 point, with correct capital letter or punctuation where needed = 1 bonus point.","Continue until all words are used."],"data":[{"word":"infrastructure","clue":"the basic systems a city needs, such as roads, bridges, water and power"},{"word":"sustainable","clue":"able to continue without harming the environment"},{"word":"pedestrian","clue":"a person who is walking in a street"},{"word":"pollution","clue":"damage to air, water or land by harmful substances"},{"word":"population","clue":"the number of people who live in a place"},{"word":"skyscraper","clue":"a very tall building in a city"},{"word":"urban","clue":"connected with towns and cities"},{"word":"commute","clue":"to travel regularly between home and work or school"},{"word":"crowded","clue":"full of people"}]},"exit_quiz":[{"q":"What type of sentence is \"Smart cities use data to control traffic.\"?","options":["compound-complex","compound","simple","complex"],"answer":"simple","explanation":"Simple sentence: one independent clause.","explanation_ar":"الجملة البسيطة."},{"q":"What type of sentence is \"The bus was late; we took a taxi.\"?","options":["complex","compound","simple","compound-complex"],"answer":"compound","explanation":"Compound sentence: two independent clauses + , FANBOYS or ;.","explanation_ar":"الجملة المركبة."},{"q":"What type of sentence is \"If the metro opens next year, my father will stop driving.\"?","options":["compound-complex","complex","simple","compound"],"answer":"complex","explanation":"Complex sentence: independent + dependent clause.","explanation_ar":"الجملة المعقدة."},{"q":"Which sentence is compound-complex?","options":["Many cars were stuck in the flood.","The streets were flooded, and cars were stuck.","The streets were flooded after the storm.","After the storm ended, the streets were flooded, and many cars were stuck."],"answer":"After the storm ended, the streets were flooded, and many cars were stuck.","explanation":"Compound-complex: two independent + one dependent clause.","explanation_ar":"المركبة المعقدة."},{"q":"","options":["The tower is tall, although, it uses very little energy.","Although the tower is tall, but it uses very little energy.","Although the tower is tall, it uses very little energy.","Although the tower is tall. It uses very little energy."],"answer":"Although the tower is tall, it uses very little energy.","explanation":"Complex sentence: independent + dependent clause.","explanation_ar":"الجملة المعقدة."},{"q":"Which word can join two independent clauses after a comma?","options":["although","because","when","yet"],"answer":"yet","explanation":"Compound sentence: two independent clauses + , FANBOYS or ;.","explanation_ar":"الجملة المركبة."},{"q":"Which sentence is NOT complete?","options":["We were waiting at the bus stop.","While we were waiting at the bus stop.","We waited at the bus stop, and the bus came.","While we were waiting, the bus came."],"answer":"While we were waiting at the bus stop.","explanation":"Complex sentence: independent + dependent clause.","explanation_ar":"الجملة المعقدة."},{"q":"How can we combine \"The building is old. It is beautiful.\"?","options":["The building is old but, it is beautiful.","The building is old, it is beautiful.","Although the building is old, but it is beautiful.","The building is old, but it is beautiful."],"answer":"The building is old, but it is beautiful.","explanation":"Combine choppy sentences smoothly.","explanation_ar":"دمج الجمل."},{"q":"","options":["The city planted thousands of trees, and the summers became cooler.","The city planted thousands of trees, the summers became cooler.","The city planted thousands of trees the summers became cooler.","The city planted thousands of trees and, the summers became cooler."],"answer":"The city planted thousands of trees, and the summers became cooler.","explanation":"Compound sentence: two independent clauses + , FANBOYS or ;.","explanation_ar":"الجملة المركبة."},{"q":"Which opening adds the most variety to \"We visited the new science museum.\"?","options":["Excited and curious, we visited the new science museum.","Visited we the new science museum.","We visited, the new science museum.","The new science museum we visited it."],"answer":"Excited and curious, we visited the new science museum.","explanation":"Combine choppy sentences smoothly.","explanation_ar":"دمج الجمل."}],"images":[{"id":"GV-L07-U5-LS4-IMG01","prompt":"Two or three of the programme characters in a scene about “Cities of the Future” that shows four sentence types: simple, compound (FANBOYS / semicolon), complex (subordinating conjunctions and relative pronouns), compound-complex; combining choppy sentences; varying sentence openings in action. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as teenagers aged 14–17, realistic proportions, modern school/city settings. Landscape 16:9.","alt":"Two or three of the programme characters in a scene about “Cities of the Future” that shows four sentence types: simple, compound (FANBOYS / semicolon), complex (subordinating conjunctions and relative pronouns), compound-complex; combining choppy sentences; varying sentence openings in action"},{"id":"GV-L07-U5-LS4-IMG02","prompt":"friendly editing-desk scene: a magnifying glass over a page with highlighted punctuation marks, Zaki holding a green pen. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as teenagers aged 14–17, realistic proportions, modern school/city settings. Square 1:1.","alt":"friendly editing-desk scene: a magnifying glass over a page with highlighted punctuation marks, Zaki holding a green pen"},{"id":"GV-L07-U5-LS4-G01","prompt":"Card-back and board design for the classroom game “Word Builder”: Zaki the Falcon icon in the centre, Leaf Green border with navy stars. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image. Portrait 2:3.","alt":"Game card design for Word Builder"}],"audio":[{"id":"AUD-GV-L07-U5-LS4-VID","script":"Hi, I’m Zaki! Today’s lesson is “Simple, Compound, Complex: Writing with Sentence Variety”. Let’s learn four sentence types: simple, compound (FANBOYS / semicolon), complex (subordinating conjunctions and relative pronouns), compound-complex; combining choppy sentences; varying sentence openings together. A simple sentence has one independent clause (subject + verb): The metro is fast. A compound sentence joins two independent clauses with a comma + for, and, nor, but, or, yet, so (FANBOYS) or with a semicolon: The metro is fast, but it is crowded. A simple sentence has one independent clause (subject + verb): The metro is fast. A compound sentence joins two independent clauses with a comma + for, and, nor, but, or, yet, so (FANBOYS) or with a semicolon: The metro is fast, but it is crowded. A complex sentence has one independent clause and at least one dependent clause (with because, although, when, if, while, after, which, who…): Because the metro is fast, many people use it. A compound-complex sentence has two independent clauses and at least one dependent clause: Although the city is big, the metro is fast, and the buses are clean. Here are some examples. Solar panels cover the roofs. (simple) The bike lanes are safe, so many students cycle to school. (compound) The streets are quiet; most people use the metro. (compound) Be careful! Some learners say: “The city is growing, it needs more schools.” That’s not right. We say: “The city is growing, so it needs more schools.” Two independent clauses → comma + FANBOYS (not just a comma). Quick check: \"When it rains, the streets flood.\" How many clauses? Which is dependent? … Think! … Two – \"When it rains\" is dependent. Great job! Now you can say: I can name the four types of sentences.","voice":"en-US, Zaki the Falcon narrator voice (bright, friendly)","speed":"1.0"}]},{"id":"GV-L07-U5-LS5","title":"The Mystery of the Empty Street: Language in Use","objectives":["Students will be able to make deductions about places and events using evidence.","Students will be able to write a description of a future city with deductions, compound nouns and varied sentences.","I can describe a city and guess what is happening there.","I can write a description with all four sentence types."],"objectives_ar":["سيتمكن الطلاب من الاستنتاج عن الأماكن والأحداث باستخدام الأدلة.","سيتمكن الطلاب من كتابة وصف لمدينة مستقبلية بالاستنتاجات والأسماء المركبة والجمل المتنوعة.","أستطيع أن أصف مدينة وأخمّن ما يحدث فيها.","أستطيع أن أكتب وصفًا بالأنواع الأربعة للجمل."],"vocabulary":[{"word":"urban","pos":"adjective","ipa":"/ˈɝbən/","definition":"connected with towns and cities","arabic":"حضري / مدني","example":"Urban areas are growing quickly.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"population","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˌpɑpjəˈleɪʃən/","definition":"the number of people who live in a place","arabic":"عدد السكان","example":"The population of Riyadh is more than seven million.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"infrastructure","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˌɪnfrəˈstrʌktʃɚ/","definition":"the basic systems a city needs, such as roads, bridges, water and power","arabic":"البنية التحتية","example":"Good infrastructure makes life easier.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"sustainable","pos":"adjective","ipa":"/səˈsteɪnəbəl/","definition":"able to continue without harming the environment","arabic":"مستدام","example":"We need sustainable sources of energy.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"skyscraper","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈskaɪˌskreɪpɚ/","definition":"a very tall building in a city","arabic":"ناطحة سحاب","example":"Dubai has some of the tallest skyscrapers in the world.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"traffic jam","pos":"noun phrase","ipa":"/ˈtræfɪk dʒæm/","definition":"a long line of cars that can't move or move very slowly","arabic":"ازدحام مروري","example":"We were stuck in a traffic jam for an hour.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"public transportation","pos":"noun phrase","ipa":"/ˈpʌblɪk ˌtrænspɚˈteɪʃən/","definition":"buses, trains and metros that everyone can use","arabic":"المواصلات العامة","example":"Public transportation reduces pollution.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"pedestrian","pos":"noun","ipa":"/pəˈdɛstriən/","definition":"a person who is walking in a street","arabic":"المشاة / راجل","example":"This street is only for pedestrians.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"commute","pos":"verb","ipa":"/kəˈmjut/","definition":"to travel regularly between home and work or school","arabic":"يتنقّل يوميًّا","example":"My father commutes to Jeddah every day.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"pollution","pos":"noun","ipa":"/pəˈluʃən/","definition":"damage to air, water or land by harmful substances","arabic":"التلوّث","example":"Cars are a major cause of air pollution.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"solar panel","pos":"noun phrase","ipa":"/ˈsoʊlɚ ˈpænəl/","definition":"a flat panel that turns sunlight into electricity","arabic":"لوح شمسي","example":"Our school has solar panels on the roof.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"crowded","pos":"adjective","ipa":"/ˈkraʊdəd/","definition":"full of people","arabic":"مزدحم","example":"The market is very crowded before Eid.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"vertical farm","pos":"noun phrase","ipa":"/ˈvɝtɪkəl fɑrm/","definition":"a building where crops grow on many floors","arabic":"مزرعة عمودية","example":"A vertical farm uses very little water.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"smart city","pos":"noun phrase","ipa":"/smɑrt ˈsɪti/","definition":"a city that uses technology and data to work better","arabic":"مدينة ذكية","example":"In a smart city, traffic lights change with the traffic.","image_id":"","audio_id":""}],"explanation":{"text":"Today you use all of Unit 5: present deduction (must be, might be, can't be), past deduction (must have been, can't have seen), urban compound nouns and sentence variety.\nA good description mixes sentence types, uses precise city words and makes guesses from evidence, which keeps the reader curious.\n✔ must / might / can't + base verb (now)\n✔ must have / might have / can't have + past participle (past)\n✔ traffic jam, parking lot, rush hour, sidewalk, solar panel\n✔ simple • compound • complex • compound-complex","examples":["The tower must be at least a hundred floors high.","The workers must have used special machines.","Someone might be living on the top floor.","There are no cars, so the city must have an excellent metro.","The sidewalks are wide, and trees shade every bike lane.","Because the roofs are covered in solar panels, the city produces its own power.","Although it is in the desert, the city is green, and the air is cool.","Rooftop gardens grow fruit for the neighborhood."],"common_errors":["✗ People must be inside yesterday. → ✓ People must have been inside yesterday. (Past → must have been.)","✗ There were no traffic jam. → ✓ There were no traffic jams. (Plural on the main noun.)","✗ The streets were empty, I was surprised. → ✓ The streets were empty, and I was surprised. (Comma splice → add a conjunction.)"],"arabic":"نراجع الاستنتاج عن الحاضر والماضي والأسماء المركبة للمدينة وتنويع الجمل.\nالوصف الجيد ينوّع أنواع الجمل، ويستخدم كلمات دقيقة، ويستنتج من الأدلة فيشوّق القارئ.\nتذكّر: must be للحاضر وmust have been للماضي، والجمع على الكلمة الأساسية في الاسم المركب."},"video":{"script":[{"time":"00:00–00:20","narration":"Hi, I’m Zaki! Today’s lesson is “The Mystery of the Empty Street: Language in Use”. Let’s learn modals of deduction (present and past), urban compound nouns, sentence variety (unit review) together.","on_screen":"GV-L07-U5-LS5 | The Mystery of the Empty Street: Language in Use","visual":"Zaki the Falcon flies in over the Leaf Green title card and lands next to the lesson title; soft chime."},{"time":"00:20–00:45","narration":"Let’s use everything from this unit. Your task: City detectives: each group gets a picture of a strange city scene (an empty highway, a crowded rooftop, a flooded tunnel, a robot at a bus stop). Groups write four deductions (two present, two past) and present them; other groups agree or disagree with evidence.","on_screen":"Language in use","visual":"Split screen: two cast members talking, with speech bubbles appearing."},{"time":"00:45–01:30","narration":"Today you use all of Unit 5: present deduction (must be, might be, can't be), past deduction (must have been, can't have seen), urban compound nouns and sentence variety. A good description mixes sentence types, uses precise city words and makes guesses from evidence, which keeps the reader curious.","on_screen":"✔ must / might / can't + base verb (now) • ✔ must have / might have / can't have + past participle (past) • ✔ traffic jam, parking lot, rush hour, sidewalk, solar panel","visual":"Grammar box builds line by line (form → meaning → use); Zaki points to each line."},{"time":"01:30–02:15","narration":"Here are some examples. The tower must be at least a hundred floors high. The workers must have used special machines. Someone might be living on the top floor.","on_screen":"The tower must be at least a hundred floors high. / The workers must have used special machines. / Someone might be living on the top floor.","visual":"Each example appears on a card with a small picture; the target part bounces once and turns green."},{"time":"02:15–02:45","narration":"Be careful! Some learners say: “People must be inside yesterday.” That’s not right. We say: “People must have been inside yesterday.” Past → must have been.","on_screen":"✗ People must be inside yesterday.   ✓ People must have been inside yesterday.","visual":"A red cross stamps the wrong sentence; it slides away and the correct sentence appears with a green tick."},{"time":"02:45–03:05","narration":"Quick check: what is wrong with “There were no traffic jam.”? … Think! … It should be “There were no traffic jams.”. Great job! Now you can say: I can describe a city and guess what is happening there.","on_screen":"Quick check ✔  |  I can: I can describe a city and guess what is happening there.","visual":"Three-second pause with a countdown ring; Zaki gives a wing \"thumbs up\" and confetti in the programme colours."}],"captions_ar":["مرحبًا، أنا زكي! درس اليوم: modals of deduction (present and past), urban compound nouns, sentence variety (unit review).","استمع وانتبه إلى الكلمات الملوّنة بالأخضر.","نراجع الاستنتاج عن الحاضر والماضي والأسماء المركبة للمدينة وتنويع الجمل.","لاحظ الأمثلة: الجزء الملوّن هو القاعدة.","انتبه! الخطأ: People must be inside yesterday. — الصحيح: People must have been inside yesterday.","سؤال سريع… فكّر ثم أجب. أحسنت! الآن تستطيع: أستطيع أن أصف مدينة وأخمّن ما يحدث فيها."]},"texts":[{"type":"model","title":"The Mystery of the Empty Street – Yusuf","body":"When I visited my uncle's new smart city last winter, I noticed something strange: the streets were almost empty at rush hour.\nThere were no traffic jams, and I couldn't see a single parking lot.\nPeople must have been inside the buildings, or they might have been using the underground metro.\nThen I saw small electric pods moving along a track, so the city must use driverless transportation.\nMy uncle, who works as an engineer there, smiled at my guesses.\n\"You can't have seen the vertical farms yet,\" he said, \"because they're on the other side of town.\"\nAlthough the city felt quiet, it was full of life underground and on the rooftops.","word_count":113,"audio_id":"AUD-GV-L07-U5-LS5-T1"}],"activities":[{"id":"GV-L07-U5-LS5-A1","type":"true_false","instructions":"Controlled practice: Read Yusuf's description. True or False?","items":[{"q":"Yusuf visited his uncle's smart city last summer.","options":["True","False"],"answer":"False","explanation":"Check the text “The Mystery of the Empty Street – Yusuf”.","explanation_ar":"ارجع إلى النص وابحث عن الجملة التي تعطي الإجابة."},{"q":"The streets were almost empty at rush hour.","options":["True","False"],"answer":"True","explanation":"Check the text “The Mystery of the Empty Street – Yusuf”.","explanation_ar":"ارجع إلى النص وابحث عن الجملة التي تعطي الإجابة."},{"q":"Yusuf saw many parking lots.","options":["True","False"],"answer":"False","explanation":"Check the text “The Mystery of the Empty Street – Yusuf”.","explanation_ar":"ارجع إلى النص وابحث عن الجملة التي تعطي الإجابة."},{"q":"Yusuf thinks the city must use driverless transportation.","options":["True","False"],"answer":"True","explanation":"Check the text “The Mystery of the Empty Street – Yusuf”.","explanation_ar":"ارجع إلى النص وابحث عن الجملة التي تعطي الإجابة."},{"q":"Yusuf's uncle works as an engineer in the city.","options":["True","False"],"answer":"True","explanation":"Check the text “The Mystery of the Empty Street – Yusuf”.","explanation_ar":"ارجع إلى النص وابحث عن الجملة التي تعطي الإجابة."},{"q":"Yusuf had already seen the vertical farms.","options":["True","False"],"answer":"False","explanation":"Check the text “The Mystery of the Empty Street – Yusuf”.","explanation_ar":"ارجع إلى النص وابحث عن الجملة التي تعطي الإجابة."}]},{"id":"GV-L07-U5-LS5-B1","type":"mcq","instructions":"Guided practice: Choose the correct answer.","items":[{"q":"People ___ inside the buildings at rush hour.","options":["must have been","must been","must be yesterday","can't have be"],"answer":"must have been","explanation":"Modal of deduction (present or past).","explanation_ar":"فعل الاستنتاج."},{"q":"There were small pods on a track, so the city ___ driverless transportation.","options":["mustn't use","can't use","must use","must to use"],"answer":"must use","explanation":"Modal of deduction (present or past).","explanation_ar":"فعل الاستنتاج."},{"q":"\"You ___ the vertical farms yet,\" his uncle said.","options":["can't seen","must have seen","mustn't see","can't have seen"],"answer":"can't have seen","explanation":"Modal of deduction (present or past).","explanation_ar":"فعل الاستنتاج."},{"q":"There were no traffic ___ in the city.","options":["jams","jamming","jammed","jam"],"answer":"jams","explanation":"Urban compound noun.","explanation_ar":"الاسم المركب."},{"q":"What type of sentence is \"There were no traffic jams, and I couldn't see a single parking lot.\"?","options":["compound-complex","compound","simple","complex"],"answer":"compound","explanation":"Sentence type and variety.","explanation_ar":"نوع الجملة."},{"q":"What type of sentence is \"Although the city felt quiet, it was full of life underground and on the rooftops.\"?","options":["compound-complex","compound","simple","complex"],"answer":"complex","explanation":"Sentence type and variety.","explanation_ar":"نوع الجملة."}]},{"id":"GV-L07-U5-LS5-C1","type":"open","instructions":"Freer practice: City detectives: write your notes.","items":[{"q":"Describe your picture in one simple sentence.","options":[],"answer":"There is a robot at a bus stop.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses modals of deduction (present and past), urban compound nouns, sentence variety (unit review) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Write one present deduction with must or might.","options":[],"answer":"The robot might be waiting for its owner.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses modals of deduction (present and past), urban compound nouns, sentence variety (unit review) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Write one past deduction with must have or can't have.","options":[],"answer":"Someone must have programmed it to take the bus.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses modals of deduction (present and past), urban compound nouns, sentence variety (unit review) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Write one compound sentence about the picture.","options":[],"answer":"The robot is holding a ticket, but the bus hasn't arrived.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses modals of deduction (present and past), urban compound nouns, sentence variety (unit review) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Write one complex sentence about the picture.","options":[],"answer":"When the bus comes, the robot will probably get on.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses modals of deduction (present and past), urban compound nouns, sentence variety (unit review) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."}]},{"id":"GV-L07-U5-LS5-D1","type":"open","instructions":"Production: Write your future city description.","items":[{"q":"Plan: name of the city, 4 compound nouns, 2 present deductions, 1 past deduction, 4 sentence types.","options":[],"answer":"Green Dune City; solar panels, bike lanes, vertical farms, metro station; must be cool inside, might be very quiet; must have cost billions","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses modals of deduction (present and past), urban compound nouns, sentence variety (unit review) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Write your description in 7–8 sentences.","options":[],"answer":"Green Dune City rises from the desert like a giant garden. Every rooftop has solar panels, and every street has a bike lane. Because there are vertical farms on every block, people eat fresh vegetables daily. The metro stations are underground, so the streets are quiet. It must be cool inside the buildings, although the temperature outside is 45°C. The city must have cost billions of riyals. When I see it, I feel proud and excited about the future.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses modals of deduction (present and past), urban compound nouns, sentence variety (unit review) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Check: present or past deduction? plural on compound nouns? four sentence types? Fix one mistake.","options":[],"answer":"I changed \"The city must cost billions last year\" to \"The city must have cost billions\".","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses modals of deduction (present and past), urban compound nouns, sentence variety (unit review) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."}]}],"game":{"name":"Quiz Show Challenge","mechanic":"timed_quiz","rules":["Teams take turns choosing a category and a cue word.","Grammar: make a sentence with modals of deduction (present and past), urban compound nouns, sentence variety (unit review). Words: give the meaning. Spelling: spell it. Write It!: write a sentence with correct punctuation.","Correct answers score 10 points; teams may steal a question another team misses.","The highest score after 8 minutes wins."],"data":[{"cue":"urban","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"population","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"infrastructure","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"sustainable","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"skyscraper","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"traffic jam","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"public transportation","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"pedestrian","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"commute","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"pollution","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"solar panel","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"crowded","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"vertical farm","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"smart city","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]}]},"exit_quiz":[{"q":"Look at the long line at the metro station. There ___ a problem with the trains.","options":["mustn't be","must be","must to be","can't be"],"answer":"must be","explanation":"Modal of deduction (present or past).","explanation_ar":"فعل الاستنتاج."},{"q":"The tower was finished in only two years. The engineers ___ very hard.","options":["must work","must worked","can't have worked","must have worked"],"answer":"must have worked","explanation":"Modal of deduction (present or past).","explanation_ar":"فعل الاستنتاج."},{"q":"It ___ rush hour. The roads are completely empty.","options":["must be","mustn't be","can't been","can't be"],"answer":"can't be","explanation":"Modal of deduction (present or past).","explanation_ar":"فعل الاستنتاج."},{"q":"Every morning, I wait at the ___ near my house.","options":["stop bus","bus-stops","bus stop","busstop"],"answer":"bus stop","explanation":"Urban compound noun.","explanation_ar":"الاسم المركب."},{"q":"Our city needs more ___ so children can play outside.","options":["greens spaces","green spaces","spaces green","green space"],"answer":"green spaces","explanation":"Urban compound noun.","explanation_ar":"الاسم المركب."},{"q":"What type of sentence is \"Riyadh is a huge city.\"?","options":["complex","simple","compound-complex","compound"],"answer":"simple","explanation":"Sentence type and variety.","explanation_ar":"نوع الجملة."},{"q":"","options":["Because the city has a metro, fewer people drive, and the air is cleaner.","Because the city has a metro. Fewer people drive, and the air is cleaner.","Because the city has a metro, fewer people drive, the air is cleaner.","Because the city has a metro, but fewer people drive, and the air is cleaner."],"answer":"Because the city has a metro, fewer people drive, and the air is cleaner.","explanation":"Sentence type and variety.","explanation_ar":"نوع الجملة."},{"q":"My cousin isn't answering. He ___ his phone at home.","options":["might left","must leave yesterday","might have left","might have leave"],"answer":"might have left","explanation":"Modal of deduction (present or past).","explanation_ar":"فعل الاستنتاج."},{"q":"","options":["Although the streets are crowded. The city feels safe.","Although the streets are crowded, but the city feels safe.","Although the streets are crowded, the city feels safe.","The streets are crowded although, the city feels safe."],"answer":"Although the streets are crowded, the city feels safe.","explanation":"Sentence type and variety.","explanation_ar":"نوع الجملة."},{"q":"Pick the best sentence for a city description:","options":["Because the rooftops are covered in solar panels, the city must produce most of its own power.","Because the rooftops are covered in solar panel, the city must produces most of its own power.","Because the rooftops are covered in solar panels. The city must produce its own power.","The rooftops are covered in solar panels, the city must to produce its own power."],"answer":"Because the rooftops are covered in solar panels, the city must produce most of its own power.","explanation":"Modal of deduction (present or past).","explanation_ar":"فعل الاستنتاج."}],"images":[{"id":"GV-L07-U5-LS5-IMG01","prompt":"A quiet smart-city street at rush hour: no cars, small electric pods on a raised track, rooftop gardens, solar panels and a metro entrance; Yusuf looking puzzled and his uncle, an engineer with a hard hat, smiling. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as teenagers aged 14–17, realistic proportions, modern school/city settings. Landscape 16:9.","alt":"A quiet smart-city street at rush hour: no cars, small electric pods on a raised track, rooftop gardens, solar panels and a metro entrance; Yusuf looking puzzled and his uncle, an engineer with a hard hat, smiling"},{"id":"GV-L07-U5-LS5-IMG02","prompt":"two programme characters doing the speaking task about “Cities of the Future”, speech bubbles left empty. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as teenagers aged 14–17, realistic proportions, modern school/city settings. Square 1:1.","alt":"two programme characters doing the speaking task about “Cities of the Future”, speech bubbles left empty"},{"id":"GV-L07-U5-LS5-G01","prompt":"Card-back and board design for the classroom game “Quiz Show Challenge”: Zaki the Falcon icon in the centre, Leaf Green border with navy stars. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image. Portrait 2:3.","alt":"Game card design for Quiz Show Challenge"}],"audio":[{"id":"AUD-GV-L07-U5-LS5-T1","script":"When I visited my uncle's new smart city last winter, I noticed something strange: the streets were almost empty at rush hour. There were no traffic jams, and I couldn't see a single parking lot. People must have been inside the buildings, or they might have been using the underground metro. Then I saw small electric pods moving along a track, so the city must use driverless transportation. My uncle, who works as an engineer there, smiled at my guesses. \"You can't have seen the vertical farms yet,\" he said, \"because they're on the other side of town.\" Although the city felt quiet, it was full of life underground and on the rooftops.","voice":"en-US, natural young-adult voice","speed":"1.0"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L07-U5-LS5-VID","script":"Hi, I’m Zaki! Today’s lesson is “The Mystery of the Empty Street: Language in Use”. Let’s learn modals of deduction (present and past), urban compound nouns, sentence variety (unit review) together. Let’s use everything from this unit. Your task: City detectives: each group gets a picture of a strange city scene (an empty highway, a crowded rooftop, a flooded tunnel, a robot at a bus stop). Groups write four deductions (two present, two past) and present them; other groups agree or disagree with evidence. Today you use all of Unit 5: present deduction (must be, might be, can't be), past deduction (must have been, can't have seen), urban compound nouns and sentence variety. A good description mixes sentence types, uses precise city words and makes guesses from evidence, which keeps the reader curious. Here are some examples. The tower must be at least a hundred floors high. The workers must have used special machines. Someone might be living on the top floor. Be careful! Some learners say: “People must be inside yesterday.” That’s not right. We say: “People must have been inside yesterday.” Past → must have been. Quick check: what is wrong with “There were no traffic jam.”? … Think! … It should be “There were no traffic jams.”. Great job! Now you can say: I can describe a city and guess what is happening there.","voice":"en-US, Zaki the Falcon narrator voice (bright, friendly)","speed":"1.0"}]}],"unit_test":[{"q":"There are cranes everywhere. They ___ a new stadium.","options":["must building","must be building","can't be building","must build yesterday"],"answer":"must be building","explanation":"Action now → modal + be + -ing.","explanation_ar":"الحدث الجاري ← be + ing."},{"q":"That ___ the new hospital. It's still a construction site.","options":["has to be","must be","can't be","mustn't be"],"answer":"can't be","explanation":"Sure it's not true → can't.","explanation_ar":"can't للتأكد من النفي."},{"q":"I'm not sure where Faisal is. He ___ at the mosque.","options":["can be","must to be","might be","mights be"],"answer":"might be","explanation":"Possible → might / may / could.","explanation_ar":"might وmay وcould للاحتمال."},{"q":"Rakan works twelve hours a day. He ___ exhausted.","options":["must be","might not be","can't be","mustn't be"],"answer":"must be","explanation":"Strong evidence → must (I'm sure it's true).","explanation_ar":"must للتأكد من الإثبات."},{"q":"Which sentence is a deduction?","options":["You can't park in front of the gate.","You must wear a helmet.","You mustn't run near the pool.","It can't be true – I saw him yesterday."],"answer":"It can't be true – I saw him yesterday.","explanation":"Not mustn't or can for deduction.","explanation_ar":"لا mustn't ولا can للاستنتاج."},{"q":"The grass is wet, but it didn't rain. Someone ___ the garden.","options":["can't have watered","must have watered","must water yesterday","must watered"],"answer":"must have watered","explanation":"Sure it happened → must have + past participle.","explanation_ar":"must have."},{"q":"Noura ___ the book already. She only bought it this morning.","options":["must have finished","might finish","can't have finished","can't finish yesterday"],"answer":"can't have finished","explanation":"Sure it didn't happen → can't have / couldn't have.","explanation_ar":"can't have."},{"q":"I can't find my wallet. I ___ it at the restaurant.","options":["might have dropped","might drop yesterday","must dropped","might have drop"],"answer":"might have dropped","explanation":"Possibly happened → might / may / could have.","explanation_ar":"might have."},{"q":"","options":["They must have be very proud of their son.","They must been very proud of their son.","They must had been very proud of their son.","They must have been very proud of their son."],"answer":"They must have been very proud of their son.","explanation":"have + past participle (been, gone, seen).","explanation_ar":"have + التصريف الثالث."},{"q":"Which sentence is about the past?","options":["The workers must be finishing now.","The workers can't be here.","The workers must have finished early.","The workers must finish soon."],"answer":"The workers must have finished early.","explanation":"Present (must be) or past (must have been)?","explanation_ar":"الحاضر أم الماضي؟"},{"q":"The ___ in our city turn green when no cars are waiting.","options":["traffic lights","traffic light's","traffic-lights","lights traffic"],"answer":"traffic lights","explanation":"Choose the right compound noun.","explanation_ar":"الاسم المركب الصحيح."},{"q":"My father ___ for an hour every day between Makkah and Jeddah.","options":["crowds","commutes","pollutes","populates"],"answer":"commutes","explanation":"Choose the city word with the right meaning.","explanation_ar":"المعنى."},{"q":"Smoke from factories causes air ___.","options":["pedestrian","infrastructure","population","pollution"],"answer":"pollution","explanation":"Choose the city word with the right meaning.","explanation_ar":"المعنى."},{"q":"","options":["The city built two new metros stations last year.","The city built two new metro stations last year.","The city built two new metro station last year.","The city built two new metros station last year."],"answer":"The city built two new metro stations last year.","explanation":"The plural goes on the main noun.","explanation_ar":"الجمع على الاسم الأساسي."},{"q":"Which compound noun is spelled correctly?","options":["side-walk","sidewalks lane","sidewalk","side walk"],"answer":"sidewalk","explanation":"have + past participle (been, gone, seen).","explanation_ar":"have + التصريف الثالث."},{"q":"Buses, trains and metros are all forms of public ___.","options":["transporting","transportation","transported","transporter"],"answer":"transportation","explanation":"Choose the right compound noun.","explanation_ar":"الاسم المركب الصحيح."},{"q":"What type of sentence is \"The tower is tall, yet it uses little energy.\"?","options":["compound","simple","compound-complex","complex"],"answer":"compound","explanation":"Compound sentence: two independent clauses + , FANBOYS or ;.","explanation_ar":"الجملة المركبة."},{"q":"What type of sentence is \"While the city sleeps, robots clean the streets.\"?","options":["complex","compound-complex","simple","compound"],"answer":"complex","explanation":"Complex sentence: independent + dependent clause.","explanation_ar":"الجملة المعقدة."},{"q":"Find the compound-complex sentence.","options":["When the festival began, the streets filled with people.","The streets filled with people.","The streets filled with people, and the lights came on.","When the festival began, the streets filled with people, and the lights came on."],"answer":"When the festival began, the streets filled with people, and the lights came on.","explanation":"Compound-complex: two independent + one dependent clause.","explanation_ar":"المركبة المعقدة."},{"q":"","options":["The desert is hot although, the new city stays cool.","Although the desert is hot. The new city stays cool.","Although the desert is hot, but the new city stays cool.","Although the desert is hot, the new city stays cool."],"answer":"Although the desert is hot, the new city stays cool.","explanation":"Complex sentence: independent + dependent clause.","explanation_ar":"الجملة المعقدة."},{"q":"How can we combine \"The park is new. It has a lake. Families love it.\"?","options":["Families love the new park, which has a lake.","The park is new and it has a lake and families love it and.","The park is new, it has a lake, families love it.","Because the park is new. Families love it."],"answer":"Families love the new park, which has a lake.","explanation":"Combine choppy sentences smoothly.","explanation_ar":"دمج الجمل."},{"q":"Pick the best sentence for a description of a future city:","options":["Every rooftop has a garden. Since the city green.","Since every rooftop has a garden, the city must stay green all year, and the air feels fresh.","Since every rooftop has a garden, the city must stays green all year, the air feels fresh.","Since every rooftops has gardens, the city must to stay green."],"answer":"Since every rooftop has a garden, the city must stay green all year, and the air feels fresh.","explanation":"Compound-complex: two independent + one dependent clause.","explanation_ar":"المركبة المعقدة."},{"q":"How can we fix it? \"the streets are wet it must rained last night.\"","options":["The streets are wet, it must rained last night.","the streets are wet, so it must have rained last night.","The streets are wet it must have rained last night.","The streets are wet, so it must have rained last night."],"answer":"The streets are wet, so it must have rained last night.","explanation":"Sure it happened → must have + past participle.","explanation_ar":"must have."},{"q":"\"Omar can't have taken the bus.\" What does the speaker think?","options":["Omar took the bus.","Omar isn't allowed to take the bus.","Omar almost certainly didn't take the bus.","Omar might take the bus tomorrow."],"answer":"Omar almost certainly didn't take the bus.","explanation":"Sure it didn't happen → can't have / couldn't have.","explanation_ar":"can't have."}],"theme_ar":"مدن المستقبل","essential_question_ar":"ما الذي سيجعل مدن المستقبل أماكن أفضل للعيش؟","can_do":"I can make deductions about the present and the past with must, might, could and can't, use urban compound nouns, and vary my writing with simple, compound, complex and compound-complex sentences.","can_do_ar":"أستطيع أن أستنتج عن الحاضر والماضي بـ must وmight وcould وcan't، وأستخدم الأسماء المركبة عن المدينة، وأنوّع كتابتي بالجمل البسيطة والمركبة والمعقدة والمركبة المعقدة."});
